eying (GPS/GIS) examines GNSS/GPS and GIS applications within Surveying & Geomatics. Key technical concerns include Spatial reference, interoperability, positioning accuracy, spatial analysis, with emphasis on how the contained topics are represented, analysed, and applied within their stated assumptions.', 'MSD_MODERN_SURVEYING_GPS_GIS', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_017_M01', 'Basic Concepts', '1', 'Basic Concepts examines Control volumes within Engineering Thermodynamics. Key technical concerns include Defining mechanism/properties, governing conditions, assumptions and limitations, application/performance criteria for Control volumes, with emphasis on how the contained topics are represented, analysed, and applied within their stated assumptions.', 'MSD_BASIC_CONCEPTS', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_017_M02', 'First Law', '2', 'First Law examines Energy equation within Engineering Thermodynamics. Key technical concerns include Energy conservation, work/heat interactions, property accounting, with emphasis on how the contained topics are represented, analysed, and applied within their stated assumptions.', 'MSD_FIRST_LAW', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_017_M03', 'Second Law', '3', 'Second Law examines Second-law analysis within Engineering Thermodynamics. Key technical concerns include Entropy, irreversibility, directionality, maximum performance, with emphasis on how the contained topics are represented, analysed, and applied within their stated assumptions.', 'MSD_SECOND_LAW', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_017_M04', 'Entropy', '4', 'Entropy examines Entropy generation within Engineering Thermodynamics. Key technical concerns include Irreversibility, entropy production, lost work/exergy, with emphasis on how the contained topics are represented, analysed, and applied within their stated assumptions.', 'MSD_ENTROPY', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_017_M05', 'Gas Power Cycles', '5', 'Gas Power Cycles examines Carnot cycle within Engineering Thermodynamics. Key technical concerns include Reversi