URSE_024_M03', 'Stability', '3', 'Stability examines Routh-Hurwitz and Nyquist criteria within Control Systems Engineering. Key technical concerns include Stability, pole location, feedback, robustness, with emphasis on how the contained topics are represented, analysed, and applied within their stated assumptions.', 'MSD_STABILITY', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_024_M04', 'Frequency Domain Analysis', '4', 'Frequency Domain Analysis examines Bode plot within Control Systems Engineering. Key technical concerns include Frequency response, stability margins, bandwidth, with emphasis on how the contained topics are represented, analysed, and applied within their stated assumptions.', 'MSD_FREQUENCY_DOMAIN_ANALYSIS', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_024_M05', 'Controller Design', '5', 'Controller Design examines PID control within Control Systems Engineering. Key technical concerns include Defining mechanism/properties, governing conditions, assumptions and limitations, application/performance criteria for PID control, with emphasis on how the contained topics are represented, analysed, and applied within their stated assumptions.', 'MSD_CONTROLLER_DESIGN', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_025_M1', 'Intelligent Agents', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with intelligent agents. The module addresses agents and environments, rational action, agent architectures, and utility and performance measures, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Artificial Intelligence.', 'MSD_COURSE_025_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_025_M2', 'Problem Solving and Search', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with problem solving and search. The module addresses state-space formulation, uninformed search, heuristic search, local search, and adversarial search, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Artificial Intelligence.', 'MSD_COURSE_025_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_025_M3', 'Knowledge Representation and Reasoning', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with knowledge representation and reasoning. The module addresses propositional logic, first-order logic, ontologies, knowledge graphs, inference, and reasoning under uncertainty, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Artificial Intelligence.', 'MSD_COURSE_025_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_025_M4', 'Planning and Decision Making', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with planning and decision making. The module addresses classical planning, partial-order planning, probabilistic decision making, Markov decision processes, and sequential decision making, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Artificial Intelligence.', 'MSD_COURSE_025_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_025_M5', 'Machine Learning Foundations', '5', 'Establishes the foundational models, terminology, and governing principles machine learning foundations. The module addresses learning paradigms, hypothesis spaces, feature representations, generalization, bias-variance, and learning pipelines, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Artificial Intelligence.', 'MSD_COURSE_025_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_025_M6', 'Natural Language Processing', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with natural language processing. The module addresses text representation, language models, sequence modelling, parsing, information extraction, and evaluation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Artificial Intelligence.', 'MSD_COURSE_025_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_025_M7', 'Computer Vision and Perception', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with computer vision and perception. The module addresses image formation, feature extraction, classification, object detection, segmentation, and evaluation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Artificial Intelligence.', 'MSD_COURSE_025_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_025_M8', 'AI Systems, Safety and Ethics', '8', 'Examines how the relevant components are organised into functioning systems and how their interactions constrain performance ai systems, safety and ethics. The module addresses AI system architecture, robustness, interpretability, fairness, privacy, and safety and governance, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Artificial Intelligence.', 'MSD_COURSE_025_M8', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_026_M1', 'Learning Paradigms', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with learning paradigms. The module addresses supervised learning, unsupervised learning, semi-supervised learning, self-supervised learning, and reinforcement learning, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Machine Learning.', 'MSD_COURSE_026_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_026_M2', 'Data Preparation and Feature Engineering', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with data preparation and feature engineering. The module addresses data cleaning, missing values, categorical encoding, scaling, feature selection, and leakage control, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Machine Learning.', 'MSD_COURSE_026_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_026_M3', 'Regression and Classification', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with regression and classification. The module addresses linear regression, logistic regression, regularization, decision trees, ensemble methods, and support vector machines, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Machine Learning.', 'MSD_COURSE_026_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_026_M4', 'Probabilistic and Bayesian Learning', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with probabilistic and bayesian learning. The module addresses probability models, Bayes rule, naive Bayes, graphical models, maximum likelihood, and Bayesian inference, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Machine Learning.', 'MSD_COURSE_026_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_026_M5', 'Unsupervised Learning and Representation', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with unsupervised learning and representation. The module addresses clustering, dimensionality reduction, principal component analysis, mixture models, and manifold learning, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Machine Learning.', 'MSD_COURSE_026_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_026_M6', 'Neural Networks and Deep Learning', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with neural networks and deep learning. The module addresses perceptrons, multilayer networks, backpropagation, convolutional networks, sequence models, and optimization, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Machine Learning.', 'MSD_COURSE_026_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_026_M7', 'Model Evaluation and Deployment', '7', 'Develops the analytical methods used to formulate, solve, and evaluate problems model evaluation and deployment. The module addresses cross-validation, calibration, imbalanced data, hyperparameter selection, model monitoring, and reproducibility, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Machine Learning.', 'MSD_COURSE_026_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_027_M1', 'Distributed System Models', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with distributed system models. The module addresses system models, communication models, time and ordering, failure models, and scalability, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Distributed Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_027_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_027_M2', 'Communication and Coordination', '2', 'Examines the mechanisms used to regulate, coordinate, or control system behaviour communication and coordination. The module addresses RPC, messaging, multicast, logical clocks, leader election, and distributed coordination, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Distributed Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_027_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_027_M3', 'Replication and Consistency', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with replication and consistency. The module addresses primary-backup replication, quorum systems, consistency models, consensus, and conflict resolution, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Distributed Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_027_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_027_M4', 'Distributed Transactions', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with distributed transactions. The module addresses atomic commit, two-phase commit, distributed concurrency control, serializability, and recovery, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Distributed Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_027_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_027_M5', 'Distributed Storage', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with distributed storage. The module addresses partitioning, distributed hash tables, distributed file systems, object storage, and metadata management, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Distributed Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_027_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_027_M6', 'Fault Tolerance and Recovery', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with fault tolerance and recovery. The module addresses failure detection, redundancy, checkpointing, recovery protocols, and Byzantine failures, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Distributed Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_027_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_027_M7', 'Distributed System Design', '7', 'Develops the design methods and decision criteria used to translate theory into an engineered or applied solution distributed system design. The module addresses availability, partition tolerance, load balancing, observability, and performance trade-offs, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Distributed Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_027_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_028_M1', 'Cloud Computing Models', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with cloud computing models. The module addresses IaaS, PaaS, SaaS, public/private/hybrid cloud, and shared responsibility, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Cloud Computing and Virtualization.', 'MSD_COURSE_028_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_028_M2', 'Virtualization Technologies', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with virtualization technologies. The module addresses hypervisors, virtual machines, containers, hardware virtualization, and resource isolation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Cloud Computing and Virtualization.', 'MSD_COURSE_028_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_028_M3', 'Cloud Resource Management', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with cloud resource management. The module addresses provisioning, autoscaling, scheduling, resource allocation, and capacity planning, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Cloud Computing and Virtualization.', 'MSD_COURSE_028_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_028_M4', 'Cloud Storage and Data Services', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with cloud storage and data services. The module addresses object storage, block storage, file storage, distributed databases, and data durability, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Cloud Computing and Virtualization.', 'MSD_COURSE_028_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_028_M5', 'Cloud Networking', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with cloud networking. The module addresses virtual networks, subnets, routing, load balancing, service discovery, and network security, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Cloud Computing and Virtualization.', 'MSD_COURSE_028_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_028_M6', 'Cloud Orchestration and Automation', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with cloud orchestration and automation. The module addresses infrastructure as code, configuration management, orchestration, service deployment, and autoscaling policies, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Cloud Computing and Virtualization.', 'MSD_COURSE_028_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_028_M7', 'Cloud Security and Reliability', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with cloud security and reliability. The module addresses identity and access management, encryption, isolation, resilience, and backup and disaster recovery, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Cloud Computing and Virtualization.', 'MSD_COURSE_028_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_029_M1', 'Data Center Architecture and Facilities', '1', 'Examines how the relevant components are organised into functioning systems and how their interactions constrain performance data center architecture and facilities. The module addresses site planning, rack layout, power distribution, cooling architecture, and physical security, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Data Center Operations and Infrastructure.', 'MSD_COURSE_029_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_029_M2', 'Compute Infrastructure', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with compute infrastructure. The module addresses server architectures, processors, memory, storage controllers, accelerators, and hardware lifecycle, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Data Center Operations and Infrastructure.', 'MSD_COURSE_029_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_029_M3', 'Storage and Data Infrastructure', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with storage and data infrastructure. The module addresses RAID, SAN, NAS, object storage, backup, and data protection, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Data Center Operations and Infrastructure.', 'MSD_COURSE_029_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_029_M4', 'Data Center Networking', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with data center networking. The module addresses topologies, switching, routing, load balancing, network virtualization, and high-availability design, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Data Center Operations and Infrastructure.', 'MSD_COURSE_029_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_029_M5', 'Power Systems and Energy Management', '5', 'Examines how the relevant components are organised into functioning systems and how their interactions constrain performance power systems and energy management. The module addresses UPS, generators, power distribution, PUE, demand management, and power quality, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Data Center Operations and Infrastructure.', 'MSD_COURSE_029_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_029_M6', 'Cooling and Thermal Management', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with cooling and thermal management. The module addresses CRAC/CRAH, chilled water, airflow management, heat rejection, and thermal monitoring, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Data Center Operations and Infrastructure.', 'MSD_COURSE_029_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_029_M7', 'Virtualization and Infrastructure Management', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with virtualization and infrastructure management. The module addresses hypervisors, containers, resource pools, capacity management, and infrastructure automation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Data Center Operations and Infrastructure.', 'MSD_COURSE_029_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_029_M8', 'Monitoring, Reliability and Emerging Technologies', '8', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with monitoring, reliability and emerging technologies. The module addresses DCIM, telemetry, incident management, redundancy, liquid cooling, and edge computing, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Data Center Operations and Infrastructure.', 'MSD_COURSE_029_M8', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_030_M1', 'Cement and Supplementary Materials', '1', 'Examines the constituent materials or components, their properties, and their influence on system performance cement and supplementary materials. The module addresses cement chemistry, hydration, supplementary cementitious materials, and blended cements, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Concrete Technology.', 'MSD_COURSE_030_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_030_M2', 'Aggregates and Mix Constituents', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with aggregates and mix constituents. The module addresses aggregate grading, shape and texture, moisture, admixtures, and mixing water, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Concrete Technology.', 'MSD_COURSE_030_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_030_M3', 'Concrete Mix Design', '3', 'Develops the design methods and decision criteria used to translate theory into an engineered or applied solution concrete mix design. The module addresses water-cement ratio, absolute volume method, target strength, workability, and proportioning, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Concrete Technology.', 'MSD_COURSE_030_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_030_M4', 'Fresh Concrete', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with fresh concrete. The module addresses workability, segregation, bleeding, setting, placing, and compaction, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Concrete Technology.', 'MSD_COURSE_030_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_030_M5', 'Hardened Concrete', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with hardened concrete. The module addresses strength, modulus, shrinkage, creep, permeability, and microstructure, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Concrete Technology.', 'MSD_COURSE_030_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_030_M6', 'Concrete Production and Quality Control', '6', 'Examines the mechanisms used to regulate, coordinate, or control system behaviour concrete production and quality control. The module addresses batching, mixing, transport, sampling, and statistical quality control, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Concrete Technology.', 'MSD_COURSE_030_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_030_M7', 'Durability and Special Concretes', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with durability and special concretes. The module addresses freeze-thaw, chloride ingress, sulfate attack, alkali-silica reaction, and high-performance and fiber-reinforced concrete, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Concrete Technology.', 'MSD_COURSE_030_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_031_M1', 'Site Investigation and Subsurface Characterization', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with site investigation and subsurface characterization. The module addresses borings, sampling, in-situ testing, groundwater, and stratigraphy, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Foundation Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_031_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_031_M2', 'Soil Parameters for Foundation Design', '2', 'Develops the design methods and decision criteria used to translate theory into an engineered or applied solution soil parameters for foundation design. The module addresses unit weight, shear strength, compressibility, permeability, and stiffness, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Foundation Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_031_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_031_M3', 'Shallow Foundations', '3', 'Establishes the foundational models, terminology, and governing principles shallow foundations. The module addresses isolated footings, strip footings, combined footings, raft foundations, and load transfer, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Foundation Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_031_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_031_M4', 'Bearing Capacity', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with bearing capacity. The module addresses Terzaghi theory, Meyerhof methods, Vesic concepts, eccentric loading, and inclined loads, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Foundation Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_031_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_031_M5', 'Settlement Analysis', '5', 'Develops the analytical methods used to formulate, solve, and evaluate problems settlement analysis. The module addresses immediate settlement, consolidation settlement, differential settlement, and time-rate effects, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Foundation Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_031_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_031_M6', 'Deep Foundations', '6', 'Establishes the foundational models, terminology, and governing principles deep foundations. The module addresses piles, pile capacity, group action, negative skin friction, and pile load testing, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Foundation Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_031_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_031_M7', 'Foundation Design and Construction', '7', 'Develops the design methods and decision criteria used to translate theory into an engineered or applied solution foundation design and construction. The module addresses serviceability, structural checks, ground improvement, and construction monitoring, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Foundation Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_031_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_032_M1', 'Hydrologic Processes', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with hydrologic processes. The module addresses precipitation, infiltration, evaporation, interception, runoff, and watershed processes, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Water Resources Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_032_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_032_M2', 'Hydrologic Measurement and Data Analysis', '2', 'Develops the analytical methods used to formulate, solve, and evaluate problems hydrologic measurement and data analysis. The module addresses rain gauges, stream gauging, hydrographs, frequency analysis, and data consistency, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Water Resources Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_032_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_032_M3', 'Hydrologic Modelling and Design', '3', 'Develops the design methods and decision criteria used to translate theory into an engineered or applied solution hydrologic modelling and design. The module addresses unit hydrograph, rainfall-runoff models, flood estimation, and design storms, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Water Resources Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_032_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_032_M4', 'Reservoirs and Water Storage', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with reservoirs and water storage. The module addresses storage-yield analysis, reservoir routing, sedimentation, and operating rules, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Water Resources Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_032_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_032_M5', 'Groundwater Resources', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with groundwater resources. The module addresses aquifers, Darcy law, well hydraulics, recharge, and groundwater modelling, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Water Resources Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_032_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_032_M6', 'Water Resources Systems', '6', 'Examines how the relevant components are organised into functioning systems and how their interactions constrain performance water resources systems. The module addresses allocation, demand forecasting, systems analysis, optimization, and conjunctive use, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Water Resources Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_032_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_032_M7', 'Flood and Drought Management', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with flood and drought management. The module addresses flood routing, floodplain management, drought indices, early warning, and risk analysis, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Water Resources Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_032_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_033_M1', 'Fluid Properties and Fundamental Flow', '1', 'Establishes the foundational models, terminology, and governing principles fluid properties and fundamental flow. The module addresses pressure, viscosity, hydrostatics, Bernoulli equation, and control volumes, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Hydraulics and Hydraulic Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_033_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_033_M2', 'Pipe Flow', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with pipe flow. The module addresses laminar flow, turbulent flow, Darcy-Weisbach, minor losses, and pipe networks, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Hydraulics and Hydraulic Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_033_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_033_M3', 'Open Channel Flow', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with open channel flow. The module addresses specific energy, critical flow, uniform flow, gradually varied flow, and hydraulic jumps, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Hydraulics and Hydraulic Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_033_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_033_M4', 'Hydraulic Machines', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with hydraulic machines. The module addresses centrifugal pumps, reciprocating pumps, turbines, cavitation, and performance curves, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Hydraulics and Hydraulic Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_033_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_033_M5', 'Hydraulic Structures', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with hydraulic structures. The module addresses weirs, spillways, culverts, energy dissipators, and intake structures, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Hydraulics and Hydraulic Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_033_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_033_M6', 'Transient Flow and Water Hammer', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with transient flow and water hammer. The module addresses surge pressure, elastic pipe flow, wave speed, and surge control, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Hydraulics and Hydraulic Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_033_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_033_M7', 'Hydraulic System Design', '7', 'Develops the design methods and decision criteria used to translate theory into an engineered or applied solution hydraulic system design. The module addresses network analysis, pump selection, system curves, and operational control, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Hydraulics and Hydraulic Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_033_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_034_M1', 'Minerals and Rocks', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with minerals and rocks. The module addresses mineral identification, igneous rocks, sedimentary rocks, and metamorphic rocks, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Engineering Geology.', 'MSD_COURSE_034_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_034_M2', 'Weathering and Geological Processes', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with weathering and geological processes. The module addresses physical weathering, chemical weathering, erosion, and mass wasting, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Engineering Geology.', 'MSD_COURSE_034_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_034_M3', 'Geological Structures and Discontinuities', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with geological structures and discontinuities. The module addresses bedding, folds, faults, joints, and shear zones, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Engineering Geology.', 'MSD_COURSE_034_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_034_M4', 'Engineering Site Characterization', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with engineering site characterization. The module addresses geological mapping, discontinuity surveys, rock mass description, and geophysical methods, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Engineering Geology.', 'MSD_COURSE_034_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_034_M5', 'Geological Hazards', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with geological hazards. The module addresses landslides, earthquakes, subsidence, expansive materials, and erosion hazards, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Engineering Geology.', 'MSD_COURSE_034_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_034_M6', 'Geology for Foundations and Excavations', '6', 'Establishes the foundational models, terminology, and governing principles geology for foundations and excavations. The module addresses rock foundations, slope stability inputs, tunnelling geology, and excavation conditions, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Engineering Geology.', 'MSD_COURSE_034_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_034_M7', 'Geology in Infrastructure Projects', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with geology in infrastructure projects. The module addresses dams, tunnels, roads, groundwater, and geological risk assessment, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Engineering Geology.', 'MSD_COURSE_034_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_035_M1', 'Geometric Modelling', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with geometric modelling. The module addresses wireframe, surface modelling, solid modelling, parametric features, and constraints, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within CAD/CAM.', 'MSD_COURSE_035_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_035_M2', 'Computer-Aided Design', '2', 'Develops the design methods and decision criteria used to translate theory into an engineered or applied solution computer-aided design. The module addresses sketching, assemblies, design intent, tolerancing, and design documentation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within CAD/CAM.', 'MSD_COURSE_035_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_035_M3', 'Engineering Graphics and Product Definition', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with engineering graphics and product definition. The module addresses sectioning, dimensioning, geometric dimensioning and tolerancing, and bills of materials, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within CAD/CAM.', 'MSD_COURSE_035_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_035_M4', 'Manufacturing Planning', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with manufacturing planning. The module addresses process planning, routing, tooling, setup planning, and computer-aided process planning, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within CAD/CAM.', 'MSD_COURSE_035_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_035_M5', 'CNC Programming and Machining', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with cnc programming and machining. The module addresses coordinate systems, G-code, tool paths, interpolation, and machining simulation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within CAD/CAM.', 'MSD_COURSE_035_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_035_M6', 'Computer-Aided Manufacturing', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with computer-aided manufacturing. The module addresses CAM workflows, tool-path generation, verification, post-processing, and machining optimization, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within CAD/CAM.', 'MSD_COURSE_035_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_035_M7', 'CAD/CAM Integration and Product Data', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with cad/cam integration and product data. The module addresses associativity, product data exchange, PLM, digital thread, and model-based definition, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within CAD/CAM.', 'MSD_COURSE_035_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_036_M1', 'Sensors and Transducers', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with sensors and transducers. The module addresses measurement principles, position, velocity, force, pressure, and temperature sensing, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Mechatronics.', 'MSD_COURSE_036_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_036_M2', 'Actuators and Drives', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with actuators and drives. The module addresses DC motors, stepper motors, servo drives, solenoids, and pneumatic and hydraulic actuators, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Mechatronics.', 'MSD_COURSE_036_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_036_M3', 'Embedded Controllers', '3', 'Examines the mechanisms used to regulate, coordinate, or control system behaviour embedded controllers. The module addresses microcontrollers, I/O, timers, interrupts, ADC/DAC, and real-time execution, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Mechatronics.', 'MSD_COURSE_036_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_036_M4', 'Signal Conditioning and Data Acquisition', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with signal conditioning and data acquisition. The module addresses amplification, filtering, isolation, sampling, and data acquisition, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Mechatronics.', 'MSD_COURSE_036_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_036_M5', 'System Modelling and Control', '5', 'Examines the mechanisms used to regulate, coordinate, or control system behaviour system modelling and control. The module addresses dynamic models, transfer functions, state-space, feedback, and PID control, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Mechatronics.', 'MSD_COURSE_036_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_036_M6', 'Mechatronic System Integration', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with mechatronic system integration. The module addresses mechanical-electrical interfaces, embedded software, control architecture, and system integration, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Mechatronics.', 'MSD_COURSE_036_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_036_M7', 'Testing and Reliability of Mechatronic Systems', '7', 'Examines how the relevant components are organised into functioning systems and how their interactions constrain performance testing and reliability of mechatronic systems. The module addresses verification, validation, fault diagnosis, calibration, and reliability testing, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Mechatronics.', 'MSD_COURSE_036_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_037_M1', 'Refrigeration Cycles', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with refrigeration cycles. The module addresses vapour-compression cycle, refrigeration effect, COP, and pressure-enthalpy analysis, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Refrigeration and Air Conditioning.', 'MSD_COURSE_037_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_037_M2', 'Refrigerants and Environmental Considerations', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with refrigerants and environmental considerations. The module addresses refrigerant properties, classification, safety, and phase-out and alternatives, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Refrigeration and Air Conditioning.', 'MSD_COURSE_037_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_037_M3', 'Refrigeration Components', '3', 'Examines the constituent materials or components, their properties, and their influence on system performance refrigeration components. The module addresses compressors, condensers, expansion devices, evaporators, and controls, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Refrigeration and Air Conditioning.', 'MSD_COURSE_037_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_037_M4', 'Psychrometrics', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with psychrometrics. The module addresses humidity ratio, relative humidity, psychrometric chart, air mixing, and dew point, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Refrigeration and Air Conditioning.', 'MSD_COURSE_037_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_037_M5', 'Air-Conditioning Loads', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with air-conditioning loads. The module addresses sensible and latent loads, heat gains, ventilation, infiltration, and load calculation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Refrigeration and Air Conditioning.', 'MSD_COURSE_037_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_037_M6', 'Air-Conditioning Systems', '6', 'Examines how the relevant components are organised into functioning systems and how their interactions constrain performance air-conditioning systems. The module addresses all-air systems, chilled-water systems, variable air volume, and equipment selection, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Refrigeration and Air Conditioning.', 'MSD_COURSE_037_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_037_M7', 'System Performance and Diagnostics', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with system performance and diagnostics. The module addresses COP/EER, part-load performance, commissioning, fault diagnosis, and maintenance, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Refrigeration and Air Conditioning.', 'MSD_COURSE_037_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_038_M1', 'Engine Cycles and Architecture', '1', 'Examines how the relevant components are organised into functioning systems and how their interactions constrain performance engine cycles and architecture. The module addresses Otto cycle, Diesel cycle, dual cycle, two-stroke/four-stroke, and engine configurations, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Internal Combustion Engines.', 'MSD_COURSE_038_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_038_M2', 'Engine Components and Mechanics', '2', 'Examines the constituent materials or components, their properties, and their influence on system performance engine components and mechanics. The module addresses cylinder, piston, crankshaft, valve train, lubrication, and cooling, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Internal Combustion Engines.', 'MSD_COURSE_038_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_038_M3', 'Air and Fuel Systems', '3', 'Examines how the relevant components are organised into functioning systems and how their interactions constrain performance air and fuel systems. The module addresses air intake, turbocharging, fuel injection, ignition, and mixture formation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Internal Combustion Engines.', 'MSD_COURSE_038_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_038_M4', 'Combustion in Engines', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with combustion in engines. The module addresses flame development, ignition delay, knock, combustion efficiency, and heat release, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Internal Combustion Engines.', 'MSD_COURSE_038_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_038_M5', 'Engine Performance', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with engine performance. The module addresses brake power, indicated power, efficiency, specific fuel consumption, and performance testing, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Internal Combustion Engines.', 'MSD_COURSE_038_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_038_M6', 'Emissions and After-Treatment', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with emissions and after-treatment. The module addresses NOx, particulate matter, CO, hydrocarbons, oxidation catalysts, and particulate filters, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Internal Combustion Engines.', 'MSD_COURSE_038_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_038_M7', 'Engine Control and Diagnostics', '7', 'Examines the mechanisms used to regulate, coordinate, or control system behaviour engine control and diagnostics. The module addresses electronic control, sensors, actuators, diagnostics, and calibration, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Internal Combustion Engines.', 'MSD_COURSE_038_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_039_M1', 'Material Structure and Properties', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with material structure and properties. The module addresses crystal structures, defects, diffusion, phase structure, and mechanical properties, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Engineering Materials.', 'MSD_COURSE_039_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_039_M2', 'Ferrous Materials', '2', 'Examines the constituent materials or components, their properties, and their influence on system performance ferrous materials. The module addresses steels, cast irons, phase transformations, heat treatment, and alloying, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Engineering Materials.', 'MSD_COURSE_039_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_039_M3', 'Non-Ferrous Materials', '3', 'Examines the constituent materials or components, their properties, and their influence on system performance non-ferrous materials. The module addresses aluminium, copper, titanium, nickel alloys, and selection criteria, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Engineering Materials.', 'MSD_COURSE_039_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_039_M4', 'Polymers and Ceramics', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with polymers and ceramics. The module addresses thermoplastics, thermosets, elastomers, ceramics, and processing-property relations, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Engineering Materials.', 'MSD_COURSE_039_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_039_M5', 'Composite Materials', '5', 'Examines the constituent materials or components, their properties, and their influence on system performance composite materials. The module addresses fibres, matrices, laminates, anisotropy, and failure mechanisms, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Engineering Materials.', 'MSD_COURSE_039_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_039_M6', 'Material Processing', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with material processing. The module addresses casting, forming, machining, joining, and additive manufacturing, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Engineering Materials.', 'MSD_COURSE_039_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_039_M7', 'Material Selection and Failure', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with material selection and failure. The module addresses Ashby-style selection, corrosion, fatigue, fracture, wear, and failure analysis, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Engineering Materials.', 'MSD_COURSE_039_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_040_M1', 'Units, Dimensions and Process Variables', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with units, dimensions and process variables. The module addresses SI units, dimensional consistency, concentration, flow rates, pressure, and temperature, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Chemical Process Calculations.', 'MSD_COURSE_040_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_040_M2', 'Material Balances', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with material balances. The module addresses mass conservation, component balances, basis selection, recycle, and purge, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Chemical Process Calculations.', 'MSD_COURSE_040_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_040_M3', 'Balances with Chemical Reactions', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with balances with chemical reactions. The module addresses stoichiometry, conversion, yield, selectivity, and extent of reaction, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Chemical Process Calculations.', 'MSD_COURSE_040_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_040_M4', 'Energy Balances', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with energy balances. The module addresses enthalpy, heat capacity, phase change, heat effects, and steady-state energy balances, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Chemical Process Calculations.', 'MSD_COURSE_040_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_040_M5', 'Combined Material and Energy Balances', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with combined material and energy balances. The module addresses coupled balances, process streams, heat integration basics, and degrees of freedom, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Chemical Process Calculations.', 'MSD_COURSE_040_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_040_M6', 'Process Flow Calculations', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with process flow calculations. The module addresses flowsheets, stream tables, process specifications, numerical solution, and sensitivity, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Chemical Process Calculations.', 'MSD_COURSE_040_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_041_M1', 'Fluid Properties and Flow Fundamentals', '1', 'Establishes the foundational models, terminology, and governing principles fluid properties and flow fundamentals. The module addresses density, viscosity, Newtonian fluids, hydrostatics, and pressure measurement, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer.', 'MSD_COURSE_041_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_041_M2', 'Internal Flow', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with internal flow. The module addresses laminar flow, turbulent flow, friction factor, pipe fittings, and pumping requirements, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer.', 'MSD_COURSE_041_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_041_M3', 'External Flow and Boundary Layers', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with external flow and boundary layers. The module addresses drag, boundary layers, flow separation, and pressure drop, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer.', 'MSD_COURSE_041_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_041_M4', 'Momentum Transport and Dimensional Analysis', '4', 'Develops the analytical methods used to formulate, solve, and evaluate problems momentum transport and dimensional analysis. The module addresses momentum balance, dimensional groups, similitude, and scale-up, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer.', 'MSD_COURSE_041_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_041_M5', 'Heat Conduction and Convection', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with heat conduction and convection. The module addresses Fourier law, steady conduction, transient conduction, and natural and forced convection, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer.', 'MSD_COURSE_041_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_041_M6', 'Heat Exchangers', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with heat exchangers. The module addresses LMTD, effectiveness-NTU, exchanger configurations, fouling, and design, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer.', 'MSD_COURSE_041_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_041_M7', 'Radiation and Thermal Systems', '7', 'Examines how the relevant components are organised into functioning systems and how their interactions constrain performance radiation and thermal systems. The module addresses thermal radiation, emissivity, view factors, combined modes, and insulation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer.', 'MSD_COURSE_041_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_042_M1', 'Diffusion and Mass-Transfer Fundamentals', '1', 'Establishes the foundational models, terminology, and governing principles diffusion and mass-transfer fundamentals. The module addresses Fick law, molecular diffusion, mass-transfer coefficients, and interfacial transport, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Mass Transfer Operations.', 'MSD_COURSE_042_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_042_M2', 'Gas Absorption and Stripping', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with gas absorption and stripping. The module addresses equilibrium relations, operating lines, HTU/NTU, and packed columns, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Mass Transfer Operations.', 'MSD_COURSE_042_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_042_M3', 'Distillation', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with distillation. The module addresses vapour-liquid equilibrium, McCabe-Thiele, reflux, tray efficiency, and multicomponent concepts, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Mass Transfer Operations.', 'MSD_COURSE_042_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_042_M4', 'Liquid-Liquid Extraction', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with liquid-liquid extraction. The module addresses distribution coefficients, ternary diagrams, stagewise extraction, and solvent selection, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Mass Transfer Operations.', 'MSD_COURSE_042_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_042_M5', 'Humidification and Drying', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with humidification and drying. The module addresses psychrometrics, wet-bulb temperature, drying curves, and drying-rate periods, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Mass Transfer Operations.', 'MSD_COURSE_042_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_042_M6', 'Adsorption and Membrane Separation', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with adsorption and membrane separation. The module addresses adsorption equilibria, breakthrough, membrane transport, selectivity, and permeability, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Mass Transfer Operations.', 'MSD_COURSE_042_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_042_M7', 'Mass-Transfer Equipment Design', '7', 'Develops the design methods and decision criteria used to translate theory into an engineered or applied solution mass-transfer equipment design. The module addresses column hydraulics, flooding, pressure drop, scale-up, and process integration, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Mass Transfer Operations.', 'MSD_COURSE_042_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_043_M1', 'Reaction Kinetics', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with reaction kinetics. The module addresses rate laws, reaction order, Arrhenius equation, elementary reactions, and kinetic parameter estimation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Chemical Reaction Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_043_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_043_M2', 'Ideal Reactors', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with ideal reactors. The module addresses batch reactors, CSTR, PFR, reactor design equations, and residence time, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Chemical Reaction Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_043_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_043_M3', 'Multiple Reactions', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with multiple reactions. The module addresses parallel reactions, series reactions, selectivity, yield, and reaction networks, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Chemical Reaction Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_043_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_043_M4', 'Non-Isothermal Reactor Analysis', '4', 'Develops the analytical methods used to formulate, solve, and evaluate problems non-isothermal reactor analysis. The module addresses energy balances, heat generation, heat removal, ignition, and multiplicity, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Chemical Reaction Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_043_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_043_M5', 'Residence Time and Reactor Performance', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with residence time and reactor performance. The module addresses RTD, E-curves, F-curves, segregation, and non-ideal flow, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Chemical Reaction Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_043_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_043_M6', 'Heterogeneous Reactions', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with heterogeneous reactions. The module addresses gas-solid reactions, fluid-solid systems, catalyst pellets, and effectiveness factors, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Chemical Reaction Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_043_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_043_M7', 'Reactor Design and Scale-Up', '7', 'Develops the design methods and decision criteria used to translate theory into an engineered or applied solution reactor design and scale-up. The module addresses reactor selection, mixing, heat transfer, safety, and scale-up constraints, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Chemical Reaction Engineering.', 'MSD_COURSE_043_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_044_M1', 'Process Measurement', '1', 'Develops the measurement and interpretation framework needed to obtain and use reliable evidence process measurement. The module addresses temperature, pressure, flow, level, analytical measurements, and sensor dynamics, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Process Control and Instrumentation.', 'MSD_COURSE_044_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_044_M2', 'Final Control Elements', '2', 'Examines the mechanisms used to regulate, coordinate, or control system behaviour final control elements. The module addresses control valves, valve characteristics, actuators, positioners, and sizing principles, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Process Control and Instrumentation.', 'MSD_COURSE_044_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_044_M3', 'Process Dynamics', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with process dynamics. The module addresses first-order and higher-order models, dead time, process gain, and dynamic testing, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Process Control and Instrumentation.', 'MSD_COURSE_044_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_044_M4', 'Feedback Control', '4', 'Examines the mechanisms used to regulate, coordinate, or control system behaviour feedback control. The module addresses closed-loop control, PID structure, stability, setpoint tracking, and disturbance rejection, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Process Control and Instrumentation.', 'MSD_COURSE_044_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_044_M5', 'Controller Tuning', '5', 'Examines the mechanisms used to regulate, coordinate, or control system behaviour controller tuning. The module addresses Ziegler-Nichols, Cohen-Coon, IMC, robustness, and performance criteria, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Process Control and Instrumentation.', 'MSD_COURSE_044_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_044_M6', 'Advanced Process Control', '6', 'Examines the mechanisms used to regulate, coordinate, or control system behaviour advanced process control. The module addresses cascade, feedforward, ratio control, override control, and model predictive control, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Process Control and Instrumentation.', 'MSD_COURSE_044_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_044_M7', 'Industrial Control Systems', '7', 'Examines the mechanisms used to regulate, coordinate, or control system behaviour industrial control systems. The module addresses PLC, DCS, SCADA, alarm management, cybersecurity basics, and safety instrumented systems, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Process Control and Instrumentation.', 'MSD_COURSE_044_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_045_M1', 'Magnetic Circuits and Electromechanical Conversion', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with magnetic circuits and electromechanical conversion. The module addresses magnetic circuits, induced EMF, torque production, and energy conversion, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Electrical Machines.', 'MSD_COURSE_045_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_045_M2', 'Transformers', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with transformers. The module addresses ideal transformer, equivalent circuit, losses, regulation, and tests, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Electrical Machines.', 'MSD_COURSE_045_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_045_M3', 'DC Machines', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with dc machines. The module addresses construction, EMF equation, torque, characteristics, and speed control, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Electrical Machines.', 'MSD_COURSE_045_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_045_M4', 'Induction Machines', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with induction machines. The module addresses rotating magnetic field, equivalent circuit, torque-slip, starting, and speed control, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Electrical Machines.', 'MSD_COURSE_045_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_045_M5', 'Synchronous Machines', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with synchronous machines. The module addresses EMF, phasors, synchronous impedance, power-angle relation, and excitation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Electrical Machines.', 'MSD_COURSE_045_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_045_M6', 'Machine Performance and Testing', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with machine performance and testing. The module addresses loss segregation, efficiency, temperature rise, load tests, and condition assessment, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Electrical Machines.', 'MSD_COURSE_045_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_045_M7', 'Machine Applications and Drives', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with machine applications and drives. The module addresses motor selection, braking, variable-speed drives, duty cycles, and protection, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Electrical Machines.', 'MSD_COURSE_045_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_046_M1', 'Power-System Components and Models', '1', 'Examines the constituent materials or components, their properties, and their influence on system performance power-system components and models. The module addresses generators, transformers, lines, cables, loads, and per-unit system, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Power Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_046_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_046_M2', 'Transmission and Distribution', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with transmission and distribution. The module addresses line parameters, voltage regulation, distribution feeders, and network topology, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Power Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_046_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_046_M3', 'Power-Flow Analysis', '3', 'Develops the analytical methods used to formulate, solve, and evaluate problems power-flow analysis. The module addresses bus types, admittance matrix, Gauss-Seidel, Newton-Raphson, and fast decoupled methods, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Power Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_046_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_046_M4', 'Fault Analysis', '4', 'Develops the analytical methods used to formulate, solve, and evaluate problems fault analysis. The module addresses symmetrical components, balanced faults, unbalanced faults, and short-circuit levels, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Power Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_046_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_046_M5', 'Protection Systems', '5', 'Examines how the relevant components are organised into functioning systems and how their interactions constrain performance protection systems. The module addresses relays, overcurrent protection, distance protection, differential protection, and coordination, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Power Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_046_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_046_M6', 'Power-System Stability', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with power-system stability. The module addresses transient stability, small-signal stability, rotor angle, and voltage stability, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Power Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_046_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_046_M7', 'System Operation and Emerging Grids', '7', 'Examines the operational principles and decisions required to run the relevant processes or systems reliably system operation and emerging grids. The module addresses economic dispatch, state estimation, SCADA/EMS, distributed generation, and microgrids, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Power Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_046_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_047_M1', 'Power Semiconductor Devices', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with power semiconductor devices. The module addresses diodes, thyristors, MOSFETs, IGBTs, and SiC and GaN devices, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Power Electronics.', 'MSD_COURSE_047_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_047_M2', 'Controlled Rectifiers', '2', 'Examines the mechanisms used to regulate, coordinate, or control system behaviour controlled rectifiers. The module addresses uncontrolled rectifiers, phase-controlled converters, commutation, and harmonics, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Power Electronics.', 'MSD_COURSE_047_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_047_M3', 'DC-DC Converters', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with dc-dc converters. The module addresses buck, boost, buck-boost, isolated converters, and continuous/discontinuous conduction, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Power Electronics.', 'MSD_COURSE_047_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_047_M4', 'Inverters', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with inverters. The module addresses voltage-source inverters, current-source inverters, single-phase, and three-phase, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Power Electronics.', 'MSD_COURSE_047_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_047_M5', 'PWM and Switching Control', '5', 'Examines the mechanisms used to regulate, coordinate, or control system behaviour pwm and switching control. The module addresses carrier-based PWM, space-vector PWM, switching losses, and gate drives, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Power Electronics.', 'MSD_COURSE_047_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_047_M6', 'Power Quality and Thermal Management', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with power quality and thermal management. The module addresses harmonics, power factor, EMI, thermal design, and heat sinks, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Power Electronics.', 'MSD_COURSE_047_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_047_M7', 'Applications of Power Electronics', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with applications of power electronics. The module addresses motor drives, renewable interfaces, UPS, HVDC, and EV charging, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Power Electronics.', 'MSD_COURSE_047_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_048_M1', 'Measurement Fundamentals and Errors', '1', 'Establishes the foundational models, terminology, and governing principles measurement fundamentals and errors. The module addresses accuracy, precision, sensitivity, resolution, and systematic and random error, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation.', 'MSD_COURSE_048_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_048_M2', 'Electrical Measuring Instruments', '2', 'Develops the measurement and interpretation framework needed to obtain and use reliable evidence electrical measuring instruments. The module addresses PMMC, moving-iron, dynamometer, digital instruments, and instrument transformers, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation.', 'MSD_COURSE_048_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_048_M3', 'Sensors and Transducers', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with sensors and transducers. The module addresses resistive, inductive, capacitive, thermoelectric, magnetic, and optical transducers, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation.', 'MSD_COURSE_048_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_048_M4', 'Signal Conditioning and Data Acquisition', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with signal conditioning and data acquisition. The module addresses amplification, filtering, isolation, ADC/DAC, sampling, and multiplexing, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation.', 'MSD_COURSE_048_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_048_M5', 'Measurement Systems and Calibration', '5', 'Develops the measurement and interpretation framework needed to obtain and use reliable evidence measurement systems and calibration. The module addresses traceability, calibration procedures, reference standards, and adjustment versus calibration, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation.', 'MSD_COURSE_048_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_048_M6', 'Uncertainty and Statistical Evaluation', '6', 'Develops the analytical methods used to formulate, solve, and evaluate problems uncertainty and statistical evaluation. The module addresses uncertainty components, propagation, repeatability, reproducibility, and confidence intervals, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation.', 'MSD_COURSE_048_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_048_M7', 'Instrumentation Applications', '7', 'Develops the measurement and interpretation framework needed to obtain and use reliable evidence instrumentation applications. The module addresses power measurements, energy measurement, process instrumentation, data logging, and remote measurement, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Electrical Measurements and Instrumentation.', 'MSD_COURSE_048_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_049_M1', 'Signal Representation', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with signal representation. The module addresses continuous/discrete signals, energy and power, transformations, and complex exponentials, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Signals and Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_049_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_049_M2', 'Linear Time-Invariant Systems', '2', 'Examines how the relevant components are organised into functioning systems and how their interactions constrain performance linear time-invariant systems. The module addresses linearity, time invariance, convolution, impulse response, and system properties, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Signals and Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_049_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_049_M3', 'Fourier Analysis', '3', 'Develops the analytical methods used to formulate, solve, and evaluate problems fourier analysis. The module addresses Fourier series, Fourier transform, spectra, bandwidth, and filtering, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Signals and Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_049_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_049_M4', 'Laplace Transform and System Analysis', '4', 'Develops the analytical methods used to formulate, solve, and evaluate problems laplace transform and system analysis. The module addresses Laplace transform, transfer functions, poles and zeros, and stability, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Signals and Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_049_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_049_M5', 'Z Transform and Discrete-Time Systems', '5', 'Examines how the relevant components are organised into functioning systems and how their interactions constrain performance z transform and discrete-time systems. The module addresses Z transform, ROC, difference equations, and digital-system response, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Signals and Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_049_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_049_M6', 'Sampling and Reconstruction', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with sampling and reconstruction. The module addresses Nyquist rate, aliasing, reconstruction, and quantization, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Signals and Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_049_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_049_M7', 'Applications and System Characterization', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with applications and system characterization. The module addresses frequency response, filters, modulation concepts, and signal measurement, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Signals and Systems.', 'MSD_COURSE_049_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_050_M1', 'Foundations of Environmental Law', '1', 'Establishes the foundational models, terminology, and governing principles foundations of environmental law. The module addresses environmental rights, public trust, precaution, polluter pays, and sustainable development, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Environmental Law and Environmental Governance.', 'MSD_COURSE_050_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_050_M2', 'Environmental Institutions and Regulatory Structure', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with environmental institutions and regulatory structure. The module addresses regulatory authorities, delegated legislation, jurisdiction, and environmental governance, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Environmental Law and Environmental Governance.', 'MSD_COURSE_050_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_050_M3', 'Pollution Control Law', '3', 'Examines the mechanisms used to regulate, coordinate, or control system behaviour pollution control law. The module addresses air pollution regulation, water pollution regulation, waste regulation, and consent mechanisms, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Environmental Law and Environmental Governance.', 'MSD_COURSE_050_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_050_M4', 'Environmental Liability and Enforcement', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with environmental liability and enforcement. The module addresses strict liability, environmental compensation, penalties, remediation, and compliance, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Environmental Law and Environmental Governance.', 'MSD_COURSE_050_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_050_M5', 'Natural Resources and Environmental Governance', '5', 'Examines the legal concepts, institutional mechanisms, procedures, and accountability issues governing natural resources and environmental governance. The module addresses forests, biodiversity, water resources, land use, and common resources, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Environmental Law and Environmental Governance.', 'MSD_COURSE_050_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_050_M6', 'Environmental Adjudication and Remedies', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with environmental adjudication and remedies. The module addresses tribunals, judicial review, writs, injunctions, and public interest litigation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Environmental Law and Environmental Governance.', 'MSD_COURSE_050_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_050_M7', 'Environmental Governance Practice', '7', 'Examines the legal concepts, institutional mechanisms, procedures, and accountability issues governing environmental governance practice. The module addresses permits, compliance systems, monitoring, reporting, and administrative decision-making, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Environmental Law and Environmental Governance.', 'MSD_COURSE_050_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_051_M1', 'EIA Legal Framework', '1', 'Examines the legal concepts, institutional mechanisms, procedures, and accountability issues governing eia legal framework. The module addresses statutory basis, regulatory instruments, project categories, and competent authorities, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Environmental Impact Assessment Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_051_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_051_M2', 'Screening and Scoping', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with screening and scoping. The module addresses screening, terms of reference, baseline requirements, and alternatives, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Environmental Impact Assessment Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_051_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_051_M3', 'Impact Assessment and Environmental Appraisal', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with impact assessment and environmental appraisal. The module addresses impact prediction, cumulative impacts, risk, and mitigation hierarchy, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Environmental Impact Assessment Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_051_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_051_M4', 'Public Participation and Consultation', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with public participation and consultation. The module addresses notice, disclosure, hearings, submissions, and procedural fairness, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Environmental Impact Assessment Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_051_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_051_M5', 'Environmental Decision-Making', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with environmental decision-making. The module addresses appraisal committees, conditions, reasoned decisions, and judicial review, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Environmental Impact Assessment Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_051_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_051_M6', 'Compliance and Post-Approval Monitoring', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with compliance and post-approval monitoring. The module addresses conditions, monitoring, reporting, non-compliance, and adaptive management, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Environmental Impact Assessment Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_051_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_051_M7', 'EIA Litigation and Comparative Approaches', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with eia litigation and comparative approaches. The module addresses standing, remedies, evidentiary issues, and comparative EIA regimes, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Environmental Impact Assessment Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_051_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_052_M1', 'Climate Governance and Legal Frameworks', '1', 'Examines the legal concepts, institutional mechanisms, procedures, and accountability issues governing climate governance and legal frameworks. The module addresses climate institutions, legislative instruments, executive policy, and federalism, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Climate Change Law and Policy.', 'MSD_COURSE_052_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_052_M2', 'Mitigation Law and Policy', '2', 'Examines the legal concepts, institutional mechanisms, procedures, and accountability issues governing mitigation law and policy. The module addresses emissions regulation, carbon pricing concepts, energy regulation, and sectoral measures, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Climate Change Law and Policy.', 'MSD_COURSE_052_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_052_M3', 'Adaptation and Resilience', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with adaptation and resilience. The module addresses adaptation duties, disaster risk, resilience planning, and vulnerable communities, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Climate Change Law and Policy.', 'MSD_COURSE_052_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_052_M4', 'Climate Finance and Disclosure', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with climate finance and disclosure. The module addresses climate risk disclosure, sustainable finance, fiduciary considerations, and reporting, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Climate Change Law and Policy.', 'MSD_COURSE_052_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_052_M5', 'International Climate Law', '5', 'Examines the legal concepts, institutional mechanisms, procedures, and accountability issues governing international climate law. The module addresses UNFCCC, Paris Agreement, nationally determined contributions, and transparency framework, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Climate Change Law and Policy.', 'MSD_COURSE_052_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_052_M6', 'Climate Litigation and Accountability', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with climate litigation and accountability. The module addresses rights-based claims, government duties, corporate claims, and causation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Climate Change Law and Policy.', 'MSD_COURSE_052_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_052_M7', 'Climate Policy Implementation', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with climate policy implementation. The module addresses policy instruments, regulatory coordination, monitoring, and evaluation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Climate Change Law and Policy.', 'MSD_COURSE_052_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_053_M1', 'Contract Formation', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with contract formation. The module addresses offer, acceptance, consideration, intention, capacity, and consent, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Contract Law and Commercial Agreements.', 'MSD_COURSE_053_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_053_M2', 'Contract Terms and Interpretation', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with contract terms and interpretation. The module addresses express terms, implied terms, conditions and warranties, interpretation, and exclusion clauses, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Contract Law and Commercial Agreements.', 'MSD_COURSE_053_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_053_M3', 'Performance and Discharge', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with performance and discharge. The module addresses performance, frustration, novation, alteration, and discharge by agreement, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Contract Law and Commercial Agreements.', 'MSD_COURSE_053_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_053_M4', 'Breach and Remedies', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with breach and remedies. The module addresses anticipatory breach, damages, specific performance, injunctions, and restitution, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Contract Law and Commercial Agreements.', 'MSD_COURSE_053_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_053_M5', 'Commercial Risk Allocation', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with commercial risk allocation. The module addresses indemnities, limitation clauses, guarantees, force majeure, and insurance clauses, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Contract Law and Commercial Agreements.', 'MSD_COURSE_053_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_053_M6', 'Contract Drafting and Negotiation', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with contract drafting and negotiation. The module addresses definitions, representations, covenants, schedules, and negotiation strategy, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Contract Law and Commercial Agreements.', 'MSD_COURSE_053_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_053_M7', 'Commercial Agreements in Practice', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with commercial agreements in practice. The module addresses sale of goods, services, technology agreements, confidentiality, and dispute clauses, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Contract Law and Commercial Agreements.', 'MSD_COURSE_053_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_054_M1', 'Employment Relationship and Conditions', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with employment relationship and conditions. The module addresses employment status, appointment terms, working conditions, and standing orders, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Labour and Employment Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_054_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_054_M2', 'Wages and Benefits', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with wages and benefits. The module addresses wage regulation, deductions, bonus, social security, and leave, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Labour and Employment Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_054_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_054_M3', 'Industrial Relations', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with industrial relations. The module addresses trade unions, collective bargaining, industrial disputes, and strikes and lockouts, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Labour and Employment Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_054_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_054_M4', 'Occupational and Workplace Regulation', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with occupational and workplace regulation. The module addresses workplace safety, working hours, welfare, and employer duties, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Labour and Employment Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_054_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_054_M5', 'Equality and Workplace Rights', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with equality and workplace rights. The module addresses non-discrimination, harassment, maternity protections, and reasonable workplace protections, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Labour and Employment Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_054_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_054_M6', 'Dispute Resolution and Adjudication', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with dispute resolution and adjudication. The module addresses conciliation, labour authorities, tribunals, and judicial remedies, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Labour and Employment Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_054_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_054_M7', 'Contemporary Employment Issues', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with contemporary employment issues. The module addresses platform work, fixed-term work, contract labour, remote work, and compliance systems, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Labour and Employment Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_054_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_055_M1', 'Corporate Governance', '1', 'Examines the legal concepts, institutional mechanisms, procedures, and accountability issues governing corporate governance. The module addresses company organs, governance structures, shareholder rights, and disclosure, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Corporate, Sustainability and ESG Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_055_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_055_M2', 'Directors Duties and Accountability', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with directors duties and accountability. The module addresses fiduciary duties, care, conflict management, and related-party transactions, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Corporate, Sustainability and ESG Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_055_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_055_M3', 'Environmental and Social Responsibilities', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with environmental and social responsibilities. The module addresses corporate environmental duties, labour rights, community impacts, and supply-chain responsibility, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Corporate, Sustainability and ESG Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_055_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_055_M4', 'ESG Disclosure and Reporting', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with esg disclosure and reporting. The module addresses materiality, non-financial disclosure, sustainability reporting, and assurance concepts, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Corporate, Sustainability and ESG Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_055_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_055_M5', 'Sustainable Finance and Corporate Risk', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with sustainable finance and corporate risk. The module addresses green finance, climate risk, transition risk, and due diligence, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Corporate, Sustainability and ESG Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_055_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_055_M6', 'Corporate Compliance and Enforcement', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with corporate compliance and enforcement. The module addresses compliance programs, investigations, whistleblowing, and sanctions, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Corporate, Sustainability and ESG Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_055_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_055_M7', 'ESG Legal Practice and Disputes', '7', 'Examines the legal concepts, institutional mechanisms, procedures, and accountability issues governing esg legal practice and disputes. The module addresses greenwashing, stakeholder claims, disclosure liability, and contractual ESG clauses, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Corporate, Sustainability and ESG Law.', 'MSD_COURSE_055_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_056_M1', 'Sociological Theory', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with sociological theory. The module addresses classical theory, functionalism, conflict theory, and symbolic interactionism, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Sociology.', 'MSD_COURSE_056_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_056_M2', 'Social Institutions', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with social institutions. The module addresses family, education, religion, economy, polity, and institutional change, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Sociology.', 'MSD_COURSE_056_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_056_M3', 'Culture and Socialization', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with culture and socialization. The module addresses culture, norms, values, identity, socialization, and deviance, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Sociology.', 'MSD_COURSE_056_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_056_M4', 'Stratification and Inequality', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with stratification and inequality. The module addresses class, status, gender, race/ethnicity as social structure, mobility, and poverty, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Sociology.', 'MSD_COURSE_056_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_056_M5', 'Groups, Organizations and Networks', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with groups, organizations and networks. The module addresses primary/secondary groups, organizations, bureaucracy, and social networks, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Sociology.', 'MSD_COURSE_056_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_056_M6', 'Population, Urbanization and Social Change', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with population, urbanization and social change. The module addresses demography, migration, urbanization, globalization, and social movements, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Sociology.', 'MSD_COURSE_056_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_056_M7', 'Contemporary Sociological Analysis', '7', 'Develops the analytical methods used to formulate, solve, and evaluate problems contemporary sociological analysis. The module addresses digital society, institutions and technology, comparative analysis, and mixed-method sociology, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Sociology.', 'MSD_COURSE_056_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_057_M1', 'Social Cognition', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with social cognition. The module addresses schemas, attribution, heuristics, social perception, and judgment, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Social Psychology.', 'MSD_COURSE_057_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_057_M2', 'Attitudes and Persuasion', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with attitudes and persuasion. The module addresses attitude formation, cognitive dissonance, persuasion models, and resistance, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Social Psychology.', 'MSD_COURSE_057_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_057_M3', 'Interpersonal Processes', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with interpersonal processes. The module addresses attraction, relationships, prosocial behaviour, aggression, and conflict, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Social Psychology.', 'MSD_COURSE_057_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_057_M4', 'Groups and Collective Behaviour', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with groups and collective behaviour. The module addresses group norms, conformity, obedience, group decision-making, and collective action, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Social Psychology.', 'MSD_COURSE_057_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_057_M5', 'Identity and Intergroup Relations', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with identity and intergroup relations. The module addresses social identity, categorization, prejudice, stereotyping, and intergroup conflict, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Social Psychology.', 'MSD_COURSE_057_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_057_M6', 'Social Influence and Communication', '6', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with social influence and communication. The module addresses normative influence, informational influence, communication, and misinformation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Social Psychology.', 'MSD_COURSE_057_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_057_M7', 'Applications of Social Psychology', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with applications of social psychology. The module addresses health, organizations, education, environmental behaviour, and interventions, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Social Psychology.', 'MSD_COURSE_057_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_058_M1', 'Growth and Structural Transformation', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with growth and structural transformation. The module addresses growth models, productivity, structural change, and industrialization, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Development Economics.', 'MSD_COURSE_058_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_058_M2', 'Poverty and Inequality', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with poverty and inequality. The module addresses poverty measurement, inequality measures, redistribution, and multidimensional poverty, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Development Economics.', 'MSD_COURSE_058_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_058_M3', 'Human Capital and Labour', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with human capital and labour. The module addresses education, health, labour markets, and returns to human capital, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Development Economics.', 'MSD_COURSE_058_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_058_M4', 'Institutions and Development', '4', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with institutions and development. The module addresses property rights, governance, political economy, and institutional quality, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Development Economics.', 'MSD_COURSE_058_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_058_M5', 'Markets, Finance and Development', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with markets, finance and development. The module addresses credit constraints, financial inclusion, market failures, and informal institutions, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Development Economics.', 'MSD_COURSE_058_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_058_M6', 'Development Policy and Evaluation', '6', 'Develops the analytical methods used to formulate, solve, and evaluate problems development policy and evaluation. The module addresses program design, cost-benefit analysis, impact evaluation, and randomized trials, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Development Economics.', 'MSD_COURSE_058_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_058_M7', 'International Development and Global Integration', '7', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with international development and global integration. The module addresses trade, aid, migration, technology transfer, and global value chains, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Development Economics.', 'MSD_COURSE_058_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_059_M1', 'Policy Concepts and Institutions', '1', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with policy concepts and institutions. The module addresses policy problems, institutions, actors, and policy instruments, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Public Policy and Governance.', 'MSD_COURSE_059_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_059_M2', 'Policy Formulation', '2', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with policy formulation. The module addresses agenda setting, problem definition, evidence use, policy design, and stakeholder analysis, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Public Policy and Governance.', 'MSD_COURSE_059_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_059_M3', 'Policy Implementation', '3', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with policy implementation. The module addresses implementation structures, administrative capacity, street-level bureaucracy, and coordination, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Public Policy and Governance.', 'MSD_COURSE_059_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_059_M4', 'Governance and Regulation', '4', 'Examines the legal concepts, institutional mechanisms, procedures, and accountability issues governing governance and regulation. The module addresses regulatory institutions, accountability, transparency, participation, and regulatory design, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Public Policy and Governance.', 'MSD_COURSE_059_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_059_M5', 'Public Finance and Policy', '5', 'Examines the concepts and methods required to understand and work with public finance and policy. The module addresses budgets, public expenditure, fiscal instruments, procurement, and resource allocation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Public Policy and Governance.', 'MSD_COURSE_059_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_059_M6', 'Policy Evaluation', '6', 'Develops the analytical methods used to formulate, solve, and evaluate problems policy evaluation. The module addresses process evaluation, outcome evaluation, impact evaluation, and cost-effectiveness, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Public Policy and Governance.', 'MSD_COURSE_059_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_059_M7', 'Digital Governance and Contemporary Policy', '7', 'Examines the legal concepts, institutional mechanisms, procedures, and accountability issues governing digital governance and contemporary policy. The module addresses digital public services, data governance, algorithmic decision-making, and platform regulation, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Public Policy and Governance.', 'MSD_COURSE_059_M7', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_060_M1', 'Research Design', '1', 'Develops the design methods and decision criteria used to translate theory into an engineered or applied solution research design. The module addresses research questions, theory and hypotheses, and exploratory/descriptive/explanatory designs, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Research Methods in Social Sciences.', 'MSD_COURSE_060_M1', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_060_M2', 'Sampling and Measurement', '2', 'Develops the measurement and interpretation framework needed to obtain and use reliable evidence sampling and measurement. The module addresses probability sampling, non-probability sampling, measurement scales, and instrument design, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Research Methods in Social Sciences.', 'MSD_COURSE_060_M2', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_060_M3', 'Qualitative Methods', '3', 'Develops methodological choices and evidence-handling practices for qualitative methods. The module addresses interviews, focus groups, observation, ethnography, and thematic analysis, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Research Methods in Social Sciences.', 'MSD_COURSE_060_M3', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_060_M4', 'Quantitative Methods and Data Analysis', '4', 'Develops the analytical methods used to formulate, solve, and evaluate problems quantitative methods and data analysis. The module addresses descriptive statistics, regression, hypothesis testing, and causal inference basics, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Research Methods in Social Sciences.', 'MSD_COURSE_060_M4', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_060_M5', 'Mixed Methods and Integration', '5', 'Develops methodological choices and evidence-handling practices for mixed methods and integration. The module addresses sequential designs, convergent designs, triangulation, and integration, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Research Methods in Social Sciences.', 'MSD_COURSE_060_M5', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_060_M6', 'Validity, Reliability and Research Quality', '6', 'Develops methodological choices and evidence-handling practices for validity, reliability and research quality. The module addresses construct validity, internal validity, external validity, reliability, and reflexivity, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Research Methods in Social Sciences.', 'MSD_COURSE_060_M6', 'Active'), ('MOD_COURSE_060_M7', 'Research Ethics and Integrity', '7', 'Develops methodological choices and evidence-handling practices for research ethics and integrity. The module addresses informed consent, confidentiality, research ethics review, data management, and reproducibility, with emphasis on their relationships, assumptions, analytical use, and application within Research Methods in Social Sciences.', 'MSD_COURSE_060_M7', 'Active') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO repo_subtopics (subtopic_id, name, subtopic_no, description, subtopic_sd_id, review_status, status, version) VALUES ('SUB_COURSE_001_M01_S01', 'Classes', '1', 'Classes refers to an object-oriented programming construct that defines the attributes/state and operations/behaviour shared by objects of the class. In Foundations & Linear Data Structures, the focus is on class definitions, objects/instances, attributes, methods, encapsulation, abstraction, constructors, visibility and implementation of abstract data types.', 'SSD_CLASSES', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_001_M01_S02', 'Stacks', '2', 'Stacks refers to a linear abstract data type in which insertion and deletion occur at one designated end, following last-in-first-out (LIFO) order. In Foundations & Linear Data Structures, the focus is on push, pop, peek/top, underflow/overflow conditions, array- and linked implementations, and time/space complexity.', 'SSD_STACKS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_001_M02_S01', 'Queues', '1', 'Queues refers to a linear abstract data type in which insertion is performed at one end and deletion at the other, following first-in-first-out (FIFO) order. In Linear Data Structures, the focus is on enqueue, dequeue, front/rear operations, circular queues, array/linked implementations, and underflow/overflow conditions.', 'SSD_QUEUES', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_001_M02_S02', 'Linked Lists', '2', 'Linked Lists refers to a linked linear data structure consisting of nodes that contain data and one or more links to other nodes. In Linear Data Structures, the focus is on singly, doubly and circular lists; insertion/deletion; traversal; node references.', 'SSD_LINKED_LISTS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_001_M03_S01', 'Binary Search Tree (BST)', '1', 'Binary Search Tree (BST) refers to a binary tree in which keys in the left subtree are ordered relative to the node key and keys in the right subtree are ordered in the opposite direction, according to the chosen ordering rule. In Trees & Graphs, the focus is on search, insertion, deletion, traversal, ordering invariant, height and best/average/worst-case complexity.', 'SSD_BST', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_001_M03_S02', 'AVL Trees', '2', 'AVL Trees refers to a self-balancing binary search tree in which the height difference between the left and right subtrees of every node is bounded by one. In Trees & Graphs, the focus is on balance factor, rotations, insertion/deletion rebalancing, search and height guarantees.', 'SSD_AVL_TREES', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_001_M04_S01', 'Quick/Merge sort', '1', 'Quick/Merge sort: Comparison-based sorting methods represented here by Quicksort and Mergesort, which organize elements into sorted order using divide-and-conquer strategies. In Sorting & Searching, the focus is on partitioning and recursive subproblems in Quicksort; splitting and merging in Mergesort; stability, in-place behaviour and time/space complexity.', 'SSD_QUICK_MERGE_SORT', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_001_M04_S02', 'Binary Search', '2', 'Binary Search refers to a search algorithm that repeatedly compares a target with the middle element of an ordered sequence and eliminates half of the remaining search interval. In Sorting & Searching, the focus is on sorted data requirement, iterative/recursive implementation, interval reduction and complexity.', 'SSD_BINARY_SEARCH', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_001_M05_S01', 'Collision resolution', '1', 'Collision resolution: Techniques used in hash tables to handle multiple keys that map to the same table location. In Hashing, the focus is on separate chaining, open addressing, probing strategies, load factor and clustering effects.', 'SSD_COLLISION_RESOLUTION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_002_M01_S01', 'Truth tables', '1', 'Truth tables refers to a tabular method for evaluating the truth value of a propositional or logical expression for every possible assignment of its component propositions. In Propositional Logic, the focus is on logical connectives, compound propositions, equivalence, tautology, contradiction and satisfiability checks.', 'SSD_TRUTH_TABLES', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_002_M02_S01', 'Induction', '1', 'Induction refers to a proof method in which a statement is established for an initial case and then shown to hold for the next case assuming it holds for the current case. In Proof Techniques, the focus is on weak/ordinary induction, strong induction, base case, inductive hypothesis and inductive step.', 'SSD_INDUCTION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_002_M03_S01', 'Equivalence relations', '1', 'Equivalence relations refers to a binary relation that is reflexive, symmetric and transitive, thereby partitioning a set into equivalence classes. In Set Theory & Relations, the focus is on relation properties, equivalence classes, partitions and representative elements.', 'SSD_EQUIVALENCE_RELATIONS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_002_M04_S01', 'Pigeonhole principle', '1', 'Pigeonhole principle refers to a counting principle stating that placing more objects than containers into those containers forces at least one container to contain more than one object. In Combinatorics, the focus is on basic and generalized forms, counting arguments and existence proofs.', 'SSD_PIGEONHOLE_PRINCIPLE', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_002_M05_S01', 'Trees', '1', 'Trees refers to a connected acyclic graph used to represent hierarchical or recursive relationships. In Graph Theory, the focus is on rooted trees, parent/child relationships, degree, height, depth, traversal and common tree representations.', 'SSD_TREES', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_003_M01_S01', 'Entities, relationships & constraints', '1', 'Entities, relationships & constraints: Core components of conceptual database modelling in which entities represent distinguishable objects, relationships represent associations, and constraints specify valid states. In ER Modeling, the focus is on entity sets, attributes, relationship sets, cardinality/participation constraints, keys and integrity constraints.', 'SSD_ENTITIES_RELATIONSHIPS_CONSTRAINTS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_003_M02_S01', 'Relational algebra', '1', 'Relational algebra refers to a formal procedural query language based on operations over relations, producing relations as results. In Relational Model, the focus is on selection, projection, union, difference, Cartesian product, joins, renaming and derived operations.', 'SSD_RELATIONAL_ALGEBRA', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_003_M03_S01', 'SQL queries', '1', 'SQL queries: Declarative statements used to define, retrieve, manipulate and control data in relational database systems. In SQL, the focus is on sELECT queries, filtering, joins, grouping, aggregation, subqueries and data modification statements.', 'SSD_SQL_QUERIES', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_003_M04_S01', 'Boyce-Codd Normal Form', '1', 'Boyce-Codd Normal Form refers to a relational normal form in which every determinant of a non-trivial functional dependency is a superkey. In Normalization, the focus is on functional dependencies, candidate keys, determinants, decomposition and lossless/dependency-preserving considerations.', 'SSD_BOYCE_CODD_NORMAL_FORM', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_003_M05_S01', 'Concurrency control', '1', 'Concurrency control: Database mechanisms that coordinate concurrent transactions so that their interleaved execution preserves required correctness properties. In Transaction Management, the focus is on serializability, locking, timestamps, isolation, conflicts, deadlock interaction and recovery considerations.', 'SSD_CONCURRENCY_CONTROL', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_004_M01_S01', 'Deadlocks', '1', 'Deadlocks refers to a state in which a set of processes or threads are permanently blocked because each waits for a resource or event held or controlled by another member of the set. In Processes, the focus is on necessary conditions, resource-allocation graphs, prevention, avoidance, detection and recovery.', 'SSD_DEADLOCKS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_004_M02_S01', 'Thread synchronization', '1', 'Thread synchronization: Coordination mechanisms that control the ordering and mutual access of concurrent threads to shared state. In Threads & Synchronization, the focus is on critical sections, mutexes/locks, semaphores, monitors, condition variables, race conditions and atomicity.', 'SSD_THREAD_SYNCHRONIZATION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_004_M03_S01', 'Scheduling algorithms', '1', 'Scheduling algorithms: Algorithms used by an operating system to select processes or threads for execution and allocate processor time. In CPU Scheduling, the focus is on fCFS, SJF/SRTF, priority, round-robin and multilevel scheduling; response, waiting and turnaround metrics.', 'SSD_SCHEDULING_ALGORITHMS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_004_M04_S01', 'Paging and virtual memory', '1', 'Paging and virtual memory: Memory-management techniques that divide address spaces into pages and physical memory into frames, allowing virtual addresses to be mapped to physical locations. In Memory Management, the focus is on page tables, address translation, page faults, demand paging, replacement and working-set considerations.', 'SSD_PAGING_AND_VIRTUAL_MEMORY', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_004_M05_S01', 'File allocation and organization', '1', 'File allocation and organization: Methods by which an operating system organizes files and allocates storage blocks to represent their contents. In File Systems, the focus is on contiguous, linked and indexed allocation, directories, free-space management and access patterns.', 'SSD_FILE_ALLOCATION_AND_ORGANIZATION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_005_M01_S01', 'Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU)', '1', 'Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU) refers to the arithmetic logic unit is a processor datapath component that performs arithmetic, logical and related bitwise operations on operands. In Digital Logic, the focus is on arithmetic operations, logical operations, flags/status outputs, operand width and datapath integration.', 'SSD_ALU', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_005_M02_S01', 'Reduced Instruction Set Computer / Complex Instruction Set Computer (RISC/CISC)', '1', 'RISC/CISC: Two broad instruction-set design approaches distinguished by how instruction complexity, encoding, addressing and implementation responsibilities are organized. In Instruction Set Architecture, the focus is on instruction complexity, instruction formats, addressing modes, register use, code density and implementation trade-offs.', 'SSD_RISC_CISC', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_005_M03_S01', 'Pipeline hazards', '1', 'Pipeline hazards: Conditions in a pipelined processor that prevent the next instruction from proceeding through the pipeline as scheduled. In Pipelining, the focus is on structural, data and control hazards; stalls, forwarding, scheduling and branch handling.', 'SSD_PIPELINE_HAZARDS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_005_M04_S01', 'Caches and virtual memory', '1', 'Caches and virtual memory: Memory-hierarchy mechanisms that exploit locality: caches retain frequently used data near processors, while virtual memory maps virtual addresses to physical storage. In Memory Hierarchy, the focus is on cache levels, locality, mapping, replacement, write policies, TLBs and page translation.', 'SSD_CACHES_AND_VIRTUAL_MEMORY', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_005_M05_S01', 'I/O organization and interfaces', '1', 'I/O organization and interfaces: Processor and system mechanisms used to communicate with peripheral devices and external interfaces. In I/O Systems, the focus is on programmed I/O, interrupts, DMA, buses, device controllers and interface protocols.', 'SSD_I_O_ORGANIZATION_AND_INTERFACES', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_006_M01_S01', 'Merge sort', '1', 'Merge sort refers to a stable comparison-based sorting algorithm that recursively divides a sequence and merges sorted sub-sequences. In Divide & Conquer, the focus is on divide-and-conquer decomposition, merge operation, stability and auxiliary storage.', 'SSD_MERGE_SORT', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_006_M02_S01', 'Knapsack', '1', 'Knapsack refers to a family of optimization problems that selects items under a capacity constraint to maximize total value. In Dynamic Programming, the focus is on for 0/1 knapsack, each item is selected at most once; state formulation, recurrence, dynamic programming and capacity/value constraints.', 'SSD_KNAPSACK', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_006_M03_S01', 'Activity selection', '1', 'Activity selection refers to a scheduling problem that selects a maximum-size subset of mutually compatible activities given start and finish times. In Greedy Algorithms, the focus is on compatibility, earliest-finish-time greedy rule, selection sequence and proof of optimality.', 'SSD_ACTIVITY_SELECTION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_006_M04_S01', 'Network flow', '1', 'Network flow refers to a graph-based optimization model in which flow is sent through directed edges subject to capacity constraints from a source toward a sink. In Graph Algorithms, the focus is on flow conservation, capacities, residual networks, augmenting paths, max-flow/min-cut and common algorithms.', 'SSD_NETWORK_FLOW', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_006_M05_S01', 'NP-complete problems', '1', 'NP-complete problems: Decision problems that are both in NP and NP-hard, meaning every problem in NP can be polynomial-time reduced to them. In NP-Completeness, the focus is on polynomial verification, polynomial-time reductions, NP-hardness and representative problems.', 'SSD_NP_COMPLETE_PROBLEMS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_007_M01_S01', 'Process models', '1', 'Process models: Structured approaches for organizing software development activities, deliverables and control points across a development lifecycle. In Software Development Life Cycle, the focus is on waterfall, iterative/incremental, spiral, agile and hybrid lifecycle approaches; activities, feedback and change management.', 'SSD_PROCESS_MODELS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_007_M02_S01', 'Continuous integration and delivery', '1', 'Continuous integration and delivery: Software engineering practices that automate frequent integration, verification and delivery of software changes through a controlled pipeline. In Agile & Scrum, the focus is on build automation, version control integration, automated tests, artifact management, deployment automation and release controls.', 'SSD_CONTINUOUS_INTEGRATION_AND_DELIVERY', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_007_M03_S01', 'Use cases and requirements specification', '1', 'Use cases and requirements specification: Techniques for eliciting, documenting and validating required system behaviour, qualities and constraints from stakeholder needs. In Requirements Engineering, the focus is on functional/non-functional requirements, actors, use cases, scenarios, acceptance criteria, traceability and validation.', 'SSD_USE_CASES_AND_REQUIREMENTS_SPECIFICATION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_007_M04_S01', 'Design patterns', '1', 'Design patterns: Reusable, named design solutions to recurring software design problems within a stated context and set of trade-offs. In System Design, the focus is on creational, structural and behavioural patterns; participants, collaborations, consequences and applicability.', 'SSD_DESIGN_PATTERNS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_007_M05_S01', 'Unit and integration testing', '1', 'Unit and integration testing: Testing practices that verify individual software units and their interactions with collaborating components. In Software Testing, the focus is on test cases, fixtures, mocks/stubs, unit boundaries, integration strategies, interfaces and defect isolation.', 'SSD_UNIT_AND_INTEGRATION_TESTING', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_008_M01_S01', 'Transmission media and signalling', '1', 'Transmission media and signalling: Physical means and signalling methods used to carry information across a communication channel. In Physical Layer, the focus is on copper, fibre and wireless media; bandwidth, attenuation, noise, modulation/encoding and transmission characteristics.', 'SSD_TRANSMISSION_MEDIA_AND_SIGNALLING', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_008_M02_S01', 'Framing and MAC', '1', 'Framing and MAC: Data-link mechanisms that delimit frames and control access to a shared or point-to-point communication medium. In Data Link Layer, the focus is on frame structure, error detection, MAC addressing, Ethernet, collision handling and medium-access methods.', 'SSD_FRAMING_AND_MAC', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_008_M03_S01', 'IP addressing and routing', '1', 'IP addressing and routing: Network-layer mechanisms for identifying interfaces or endpoints and selecting paths for forwarding packets between networks. In Network Layer, the focus is on iPv4/IPv6 addressing, subnetting, forwarding tables, routing principles and route selection.', 'SSD_IP_ADDRESSING_AND_ROUTING', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_008_M04_S01', 'Transmission Control Protocol / User Datagram Protocol (TCP/UDP)', '1', 'TCP/UDP: Transport-layer protocols represented by TCP, a connection-oriented reliable byte-stream protocol, and UDP, a connectionless datagram transport. In Transport Layer, the focus is on ports, multiplexing, TCP sequencing/acknowledgement/congestion control and UDP datagrams.', 'SSD_TCP_UDP', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_008_M05_S01', 'Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP)', '1', 'Hypertext Transfer Protocol (HTTP) refers to an application-layer request/response protocol used for transferring web resources and related representations. In Application Layer, the focus is on methods, status codes, headers, message semantics, caching, persistent connections and HTTP over secure transports.', 'SSD_HTTP', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_009_M01_S01', 'Hooke''s Law', '1', 'Hooke''s Law: Within the linear elastic range of a material, stress is proportional to strain for the relevant loading mode. In Simple Stresses, the focus is on normal stress/strain relation, elastic modulus, proportional limit and applicability to linear elasticity.', 'SSD_HOOKE_S_LAW', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_009_M02_S01', 'Flexure formula', '1', 'Flexure formula refers to the beam flexure relation that connects bending stress to bending moment, cross-sectional geometry and distance from the neutral axis under stated beam assumptions. In Bending Moment, the focus is on σ = My/I, neutral axis, second moment of area, bending moment and elastic-beam assumptions.', 'SSD_FLEXURE_FORMULA', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_009_M03_S01', 'Bending stress distribution', '1', 'Bending stress distribution refers to the spatial variation of normal bending stress across a beam cross-section caused by an applied bending moment. In Bending Stresses, the focus is on linear stress distribution in elastic homogeneous sections, neutral axis, extreme fibres and section modulus.', 'SSD_BENDING_STRESS_DISTRIBUTION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_009_M04_S01', 'Circular shafts', '1', 'Circular shafts: Cylindrical structural members designed to transmit torque and resist associated torsional stresses and deformation. In Torsion, the focus is on solid/hollow shafts, torque, polar moment of inertia, torsional shear stress, angle of twist and power transmission.', 'SSD_CIRCULAR_SHAFTS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_009_M05_S01', 'Beam deflection methods', '1', 'Beam deflection methods: Analytical methods used to determine displacement and slope of beams under transverse loading. In Deflection, the focus is on double integration, singularity functions, moment-area, conjugate beam and related elastic methods.', 'SSD_BEAM_DEFLECTION_METHODS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_010_M01_S01', 'Viscosity', '1', 'Viscosity refers to a measure of a fluid’s resistance to deformation and flow, arising from internal friction and relating shear stress to velocity gradient under Newtonian conditions. In Fluid Properties, the focus is on concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules.', 'SSD_VISCOSITY', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_010_M02_S01', 'Buoyancy', '1', 'Buoyancy refers to the net upward force exerted by a fluid on an immersed or floating body due to the pressure distribution in the fluid. In Hydrostatics, the focus is on archimedes'' principle, displaced-fluid volume, centre of buoyancy and floating equilibrium.', 'SSD_BUOYANCY', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_010_M03_S01', 'Continuity', '1', 'Continuity refers to the mass-conservation relation requiring that mass entering, leaving and accumulating within a fluid system satisfy conservation of mass. In Kinematics, the focus is on control-volume continuity, steady/unsteady flow, incompressible simplification and area-velocity relationships.', 'SSD_CONTINUITY', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_010_M04_S01', 'Reynolds number', '1', 'Reynolds number refers to a dimensionless ratio comparing inertial effects with viscous effects in fluid flow. In Dynamics, the focus is on re = ρVL/μ, characteristic length/velocity choices, similarity and flow-regime interpretation.', 'SSD_REYNOLDS_NUMBER', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_010_M05_S01', 'Head loss and pipe-flow analysis', '1', 'Head loss and pipe-flow analysis: Analysis of pressure or energy losses associated with fluid flow through pipes and fittings. In Pipe Flow, the focus is on darcy-Weisbach equation, friction factor, minor losses, hydraulic grade/energy lines and flow regimes.', 'SSD_HEAD_LOSS_AND_PIPE_FLOW_ANALYSIS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_011_M01_S01', 'Truss and beam analysis', '1', 'Truss and beam analysis: Structural analysis procedures for determining internal forces and reactions in idealized trusses and beams under applied loads. In Determinate Structures, the focus is on equilibrium, free-body diagrams, axial truss forces, shear and bending moment in beams.', 'SSD_TRUSS_AND_BEAM_ANALYSIS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_011_M02_S01', 'Moment-area theorem', '1', 'Moment-area theorem: Beam-deflection relations that connect changes in slope and deflection to areas and first moments of the M/EI diagram. In Deflections, the focus is on theorem 1 for slope change, theorem 2 for tangential deviation, boundary conditions and sign conventions.', 'SSD_MOMENT_AREA_THEOREM', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_011_M03_S01', 'Virtual work', '1', 'Virtual work refers to an analytical method that uses work equivalence under a compatible virtual displacement to determine structural responses. In Energy Methods, the focus is on virtual displacements, external/internal virtual work, unit-load method and displacement calculation.', 'SSD_VIRTUAL_WORK', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_011_M04_S01', 'Influence-line construction', '1', 'Influence-line construction refers to a graphical or analytical representation showing how a response quantity at a specified location varies as a moving load changes position. In Influence Lines, the focus is on influence lines for reactions, shear, moment and other responses in determinate structures.', 'SSD_INFLUENCE_LINE_CONSTRUCTION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_011_M05_S01', 'Slope-deflection', '1', 'Slope-deflection refers to a displacement-based structural analysis method relating member end moments to end rotations, translations and fixed-end actions. In Indeterminate Structures, the focus is on member stiffness, end rotations, joint translations, fixed-end moments and compatibility equations.', 'SSD_SLOPE_DEFLECTION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_012_M01_S01', 'Atterberg limits', '1', 'Atterberg limits: Empirical moisture-content limits used to characterize the consistency and plasticity range of fine-grained soils. In Soil Classification, the focus is on liquid limit, plastic limit, shrinkage limit, plasticity index and consistency states.', 'SSD_ATTERBERG_LIMITS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_012_M02_S01', 'Darcy''s law', '1', 'Darcy''s law refers to a constitutive relation stating that, under laminar saturated porous-media flow conditions, discharge is proportional to hydraulic gradient and hydraulic conductivity. In Permeability, the focus is on hydraulic head, gradient, hydraulic conductivity, discharge/flux and applicability limits.', 'SSD_DARCY_S_LAW', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_012_M03_S01', 'Consolidation settlement', '1', 'Consolidation settlement: Time-dependent settlement of a saturated or nearly saturated soil caused by dissipation of excess pore-water pressure and associated volume change under sustained loading. In Consolidation, the focus is on concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules.', 'SSD_CONSOLIDATION_SETTLEMENT', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_012_M04_S01', 'Mohr-Coulomb failure criterion', '1', 'Mohr-Coulomb failure criterion refers to a frictional failure criterion relating shear strength of soil or rock to effective normal stress, cohesion and friction angle. In Shear Strength, the focus is on τf = c'' + σ''n tanφ'' for effective-stress form, failure envelope and drained/undrained interpretation.', 'SSD_MOHR_COULOMB_FAILURE_CRITERION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_012_M05_S01', 'Lateral earth pressure', '1', 'Lateral earth pressure refers to the pressure exerted by soil against a retaining or embedded structure due to soil self-weight, surcharge, groundwater and other actions. In Earth Pressure, the focus is on active, passive and at-rest states, earth-pressure coefficients, wall friction and groundwater effects.', 'SSD_LATERAL_EARTH_PRESSURE', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_013_M01_S01', 'Demand forecasting', '1', 'Demand forecasting: Estimation of future demand for a resource or service from historical observations, explanatory variables, assumptions, and uncertainty, used to support planning and design. In Water Demand, the focus is on concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules.', 'SSD_DEMAND_FORECASTING', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_013_M02_S01', 'Filtration', '1', 'Filtration refers to a water or wastewater treatment process that removes suspended or particulate matter by passing fluid through a porous filter medium. In Water Treatment, the focus is on media filtration, straining, adsorption contributions, head loss, backwashing and filtration performance.', 'SSD_FILTRATION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_013_M03_S01', 'Sewer design', '1', 'Sewer design: Engineering design of sewer systems to collect and convey wastewater safely and reliably to treatment or disposal facilities. In Wastewater Collection, the focus is on flow estimation, pipe sizing, hydraulic grade, self-cleansing considerations, minimum/maximum velocities and system layout.', 'SSD_SEWER_DESIGN', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_013_M04_S01', 'Activated sludge process', '1', 'Activated sludge process refers to a suspended-growth biological wastewater-treatment process in which microorganisms oxidize biodegradable pollutants in an aerated reactor followed by solids separation. In Sewage Treatment, the focus is on aeration, biomass concentration, substrate removal, secondary clarification, sludge age and return/waste activated sludge.', 'SSD_ACTIVATED_SLUDGE_PROCESS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_013_M05_S01', 'Solid-waste management', '1', 'Solid-waste management refers to the systematic handling of solid wastes through generation reduction, segregation, collection, transport, processing, recovery and final disposal. In Solid Waste, the focus is on waste characterization, collection, recycling/material recovery, biological treatment, thermal treatment and engineered disposal.', 'SSD_SOLID_WASTE_MANAGEMENT', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_014_M01_S01', 'Sight distance', '1', 'Sight distance refers to the roadway length over which a driver can see an object or roadway feature sufficiently far ahead to perform a required manoeuvre safely. In Highway Planning, the focus is on stopping, passing and decision sight distance; driver perception-reaction, speed, grade and geometric constraints.', 'SSD_SIGHT_DISTANCE', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_014_M02_S01', 'Super elevation', '1', 'Super elevation refers to the transverse slope provided on a roadway curve to assist in counteracting lateral acceleration associated with vehicle motion. In Geometric Design, the focus is on superelevation rate, side friction, design speed, radius, runoff and transition.', 'SSD_SUPER_ELEVATION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_014_M03_S01', 'Traffic flow and control', '1', 'Traffic flow and control: Analysis and management of the movement of vehicles and people on transportation networks using flow relationships and control strategies. In Traffic Engineering, the focus is on flow, speed, density, fundamental diagrams, intersections, signals, capacity and control measures.', 'SSD_TRAFFIC_FLOW_AND_CONTROL', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_014_M04_S01', 'Bitumen testing', '1', 'Bitumen testing: Laboratory characterization of bituminous binders through standardized tests of consistency, viscosity, temperature susceptibility and related properties. In Pavement Materials, the focus is on penetration, ductility, softening point, viscosity, flash/fire point and temperature susceptibility, as applicable to the specification.', 'SSD_BITUMEN_TESTING', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_014_M05_S01', 'Flexible pavement design', '1', 'Flexible pavement design: Design of layered pavement systems in which wheel loads are distributed through bituminous and granular layers over the subgrade. In Pavement Design, the focus is on traffic loading, material properties, layer thicknesses, subgrade strength, drainage, fatigue and rutting considerations.', 'SSD_FLEXIBLE_PAVEMENT_DESIGN', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_015_M01_S01', 'Gantt charts', '1', 'Gantt charts refers to a time-scaled project scheduling representation showing activities, durations and their planned timing. In Project Lifecycle, the focus is on activities, durations, start/finish dates, overlaps, milestones and progress tracking.', 'SSD_GANTT_CHARTS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_015_M02_S01', 'Crashing', '1', 'Crashing refers to a schedule-compression technique that reduces activity durations by applying additional resources or cost, subject to technical feasibility. In Network Techniques (CPM/PERT), the focus is on normal/crash durations and costs, cost slopes, critical paths and incremental time-cost trade-offs.', 'SSD_CRASHING', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_015_M03_S01', 'Resource levelling', '1', 'Resource levelling refers to a scheduling process that adjusts activity timing to resolve resource over-allocation while respecting stated project constraints. In Resource Allocation, the focus is on resource availability, activity priorities, float, sequencing and schedule impacts.', 'SSD_RESOURCE_LEVELLING', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_015_M04_S01', 'Depreciation and cost control', '1', 'Depreciation and cost control: Methods for allocating the depreciable cost of assets over their useful lives and monitoring project costs against budgets. In Cost Control, the focus is on straight-line and declining-balance methods, book value, useful life, residual value, cost variance and budget control.', 'SSD_DEPRECIATION_AND_COST_CONTROL', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_015_M05_S01', 'Equipment selection and productivity', '1', 'Equipment selection and productivity: Selection and operational assessment of construction equipment based on required work, capacity, cycle time, site conditions and economic constraints. In Construction Equipment, the focus is on equipment capacity, cycle time, utilization, production rate, operating cost and site compatibility.', 'SSD_EQUIPMENT_SELECTION_AND_PRODUCTIVITY', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_016_M01_S01', 'Errors', '1', 'Errors: Deviations of measured or computed quantities from an accepted reference or true/accepted value, including systematic and random components. In Basics of Surveying, the focus is on accuracy, precision, systematic/random error, propagation, uncertainty and error detection.', 'SSD_ERRORS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_016_M02_S01', 'Benchmarks', '1', 'Benchmarks: Reference points with known or established elevations used to control vertical surveying and transfer elevation information. In Leveling & Contouring, the focus is on permanent/temporary benchmarks, datum, reduced levels, levelling networks and monumentation.', 'SSD_BENCHMARKS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_016_M03_S01', 'Angular measurement', '1', 'Angular measurement: Determination of horizontal or vertical angles between survey lines or directions using appropriate angular-measurement instruments. In Theodolite Surveying, the focus is on theodolites/total stations, centering, face observations, repetition, direction measurement and error control.', 'SSD_ANGULAR_MEASUREMENT', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_016_M04_S01', 'Horizontal and vertical curves', '1', 'Horizontal and vertical curves: Geometric transition elements used to connect roadway alignments while controlling changes in direction and grade. In Curves, the focus is on simple/compound horizontal curves, circular elements, transition curves, vertical parabolic curves and sight-distance considerations.', 'SSD_HORIZONTAL_AND_VERTICAL_CURVES', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_016_M05_S01', 'GNSS/GPS and GIS applications', '1', 'GNSS/GPS and GIS applications: Use of satellite-based positioning and geographic information systems to acquire, reference, manage, analyze and visualize spatial data. In Modern Surveying (GPS/GIS), the focus is on gNSS positioning, coordinate reference systems, accuracy/error sources, GIS layers, spatial queries and mapping.', 'SSD_GNSS_GPS_AND_GIS_APPLICATIONS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_017_M01_S01', 'Control volumes', '1', 'Control volumes refers to a defined region in space used for applying conservation equations to mass, momentum, and energy crossing its boundary. In Basic Concepts, the focus is on concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules.', 'SSD_CONTROL_VOLUMES', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_017_M02_S01', 'Energy equation', '1', 'Energy equation refers to a statement of energy conservation applied to a thermodynamic system or control volume. In First Law, the focus is on internal, kinetic and potential energy, heat transfer, work, mass-flow energy and steady-flow simplifications.', 'SSD_ENERGY_EQUATION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_017_M03_S01', 'Second-law analysis', '1', 'Second-law analysis: Thermodynamic analysis based on the second law, including entropy balance and restrictions on energy-conversion processes. In Second Law, the focus is on entropy balance, irreversibility, entropy generation, reversible/irreversible processes and efficiency limits.', 'SSD_SECOND_LAW_ANALYSIS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_017_M04_S01', 'Entropy generation', '1', 'Entropy generation refers to the production of entropy associated with irreversible processes within a system or control volume. In Entropy, the focus is on entropy balance, heat transfer across finite temperature differences, friction, mixing and other irreversibilities.', 'SSD_ENTROPY_GENERATION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_017_M05_S01', 'Carnot cycle', '1', 'Carnot cycle refers to an ideal reversible heat-engine cycle consisting of two isothermal and two reversible adiabatic (isentropic) processes between two thermal reservoirs. In Gas Power Cycles, the focus is on isothermal expansion/compression, isentropic expansion/compression and maximum reversible efficiency.', 'SSD_CARNOT_CYCLE', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_018_M01_S01', 'Velocity and acceleration fields', '1', 'Velocity and acceleration fields: Spatial and temporal fields describing fluid-particle velocity and acceleration throughout a flow domain. In Fluid Kinematics, the focus is on eulerian velocity field, material acceleration, local and convective acceleration, streamlines.', 'SSD_VELOCITY_AND_ACCELERATION_FIELDS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_018_M02_S01', 'Navier-Stokes equation', '1', 'Navier-Stokes equation refers to the momentum-conservation equation for a continuum fluid, with terms determined by density, pressure, body forces and constitutive behaviour. In Conservation Laws, the focus is on continuity coupling, pressure, viscous stresses, body forces, incompressible simplifications and boundary conditions.', 'SSD_NAVIER_STOKES_EQUATION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_018_M03_S01', 'Boundary layers', '1', 'Boundary layers: Thin regions adjacent to solid surfaces in which viscous effects produce strong velocity gradients and influence momentum, heat, or mass transfer. In Viscous Flow, the focus is on concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules.', 'SSD_BOUNDARY_LAYERS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_018_M04_S01', 'Pelton and Francis turbines', '1', 'Pelton and Francis turbines: Hydraulic turbine types represented by Pelton impulse turbines and Francis reaction turbines for converting water energy into shaft power. In Hydraulic Turbines, the focus is on pelton jet/bucket interaction; Francis runner, pressure change, head, flow rate, efficiency and operating range.', 'SSD_PELTON_AND_FRANCIS_TURBINES', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_018_M05_S01', 'Centrifugal pumps', '1', 'Centrifugal pumps: Rotodynamic pumps that impart energy to a fluid primarily through the action of a rotating impeller, converting mechanical energy into fluid pressure and head. In Pumps, the focus is on concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules.', 'SSD_CENTRIFUGAL_PUMPS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_019_M01_S01', 'Grashof''s law', '1', 'Grashof''s law refers to a kinematic criterion for planar four-bar linkages relating link lengths to the possibility of continuous rotation of at least one link. In Mechanisms, the focus is on shortest/longest/other link lengths, S+L ≤ P+Q criterion and limiting cases.', 'SSD_GRASHOF_S_LAW', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_019_M02_S01', 'Instantaneous centers', '1', 'Instantaneous centers: Points or centers in planar rigid-body motion about which the relative velocity between two bodies is instantaneously equivalent to rotation. In Velocity/Acceleration Analysis, the focus is on relative motion, Kennedy''s theorem, velocity relationships and construction methods.', 'SSD_INSTANTANEOUS_CENTERS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_019_M03_S01', 'Cam displacement diagrams', '1', 'Cam displacement diagrams: Graphs relating follower displacement, velocity, acceleration or related motion variables to cam angle or time. In Cams, the focus is on follower motion laws, rise/dwell/return, simple harmonic/cycloidal/polynomial motion and motion continuity.', 'SSD_CAM_DISPLACEMENT_DIAGRAMS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_019_M04_S01', 'Epicyclic gear trains', '1', 'Epicyclic gear trains: Gear arrangements in which one or more gears rotate about axes that themselves move relative to a fixed frame. In Gears, the focus is on sun, planet, ring and carrier elements; relative motion; speed ratios and torque relationships.', 'SSD_EPICYCLIC_GEAR_TRAINS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_019_M05_S01', 'Friction in machine mechanisms', '1', 'Friction in machine mechanisms: Resistance to relative motion between contacting machine components, affecting forces, power loss, wear and motion. In Friction, the focus is on dry/sliding friction, rolling resistance, friction laws, lubrication effects and efficiency implications.', 'SSD_FRICTION_IN_MACHINE_MECHANISMS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_020_M01_S01', 'Fins', '1', 'Fins: Extended surfaces used to increase heat-transfer area and enhance heat transfer between a solid and an adjoining fluid. In Conduction, the focus is on fin geometry, conduction within the fin, convection boundary condition, efficiency/effectiveness and temperature distribution.', 'SSD_FINS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_020_M02_S01', 'Free/forced convection', '1', 'Free/forced convection: Heat transfer between a surface and moving fluid driven respectively by buoyancy or by externally imposed fluid motion. In Convection, the focus is on natural/free convection, forced convection, boundary layers, dimensionless correlations and heat-transfer coefficients.', 'SSD_FREE_FORCED_CONVECTION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_020_M03_S01', 'Blackbody radiation', '1', 'Blackbody radiation: Thermal radiation idealization for a surface that absorbs all incident radiation and emits the maximum possible radiation at a given temperature. In Radiation, the focus is on blackbody emissive power, Stefan-Boltzmann law, spectral distribution and radiative exchange assumptions.', 'SSD_BLACKBODY_RADIATION', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_020_M04_S01', 'Log Mean Temperature Difference (LMTD)', '1', 'LMTD: Log-mean temperature difference, a mean temperature-driving-force measure used in heat-exchanger analysis when the temperature difference varies along the exchanger. In Heat Exchangers, the focus is on concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules.', 'SSD_LMTD', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_020_M05_S01', 'Mass diffusion and transfer coefficients', '1', 'Mass diffusion and transfer coefficients: Transport of chemical species caused by concentration gradients and the coefficients used to relate mass-transfer flux to a driving concentration difference. In Mass Transfer, the focus is on fickian diffusion, concentration gradients, molecular diffusivity, convective mass transfer and dimensionless correlations.', 'SSD_MASS_DIFFUSION_AND_TRANSFER_COEFFICIENTS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_021_M01_S01', 'Flywheels', '1', 'Flywheels: Rotating mechanical energy-storage elements that reduce cyclic speed fluctuations by storing and releasing kinetic energy. In Dynamic Force Analysis, the focus is on energy fluctuation, moment of inertia, coefficient of speed fluctuation and angular velocity.', 'SSD_FLYWHEELS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_021_M02_S01', 'Static and dynamic balancing', '1', 'Static and dynamic balancing: Procedures for reducing unbalanced forces and moments in rotating or reciprocating machinery. In Balancing, the focus is on mass distribution, centrifugal forces, static balance, couple balance, correction planes and balancing procedures.', 'SSD_STATIC_AND_DYNAMIC_BALANCING', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_021_M03_S01', 'Natural frequency', '1', 'Natural frequency refers to a characteristic frequency at which a system can oscillate freely after a disturbance in the absence of sustained external excitation and damping effects. In Free Vibration, the focus is on single/multi-degree systems, stiffness, mass, damping influence and mode shapes.', 'SSD_NATURAL_FREQUENCY', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_021_M04_S01', 'Resonance', '1', 'Resonance refers to a condition in which forced vibration response becomes large when excitation frequency approaches an appropriate natural frequency of the system. In Forced Vibration, the focus is on frequency response, damping, natural frequency, amplitude and phase behaviour.', 'SSD_RESONANCE', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_021_M05_S01', 'Governor and gyroscope principles', '1', 'Governor and gyroscope principles: Rotational-mechanics principles represented by governors for speed regulation and gyroscopes for angular-momentum-based orientation and reaction effects. In Governors & Gyroscopes, the focus is on governor equilibrium/speed regulation; gyroscopic moment, precession and angular momentum.', 'SSD_GOVERNOR_AND_GYROSCOPE_PRINCIPLES', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_022_M01_S01', 'Sand casting', '1', 'Sand casting refers to a metal casting process in which molten metal is poured into a mould cavity formed in compacted sand. In Casting, the focus is on pattern, moulding sand, gating/riser system, solidification, defects and post-casting finishing.', 'SSD_SAND_CASTING', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_022_M02_S01', 'Forging', '1', 'Forging refers to a manufacturing process that plastically deforms metal using compressive forces to produce a desired shape and properties. In Metal Forming, the focus is on open/closed-die forging, temperature, deformation, grain flow, tooling and defects.', 'SSD_FORGING', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_022_M03_S01', 'Arc welding', '1', 'Arc welding refers to a fusion welding process in which an electric arc supplies heat to melt and join materials, with or without filler metal. In Joining Processes, the focus is on arc generation, electrodes, shielding, heat input, joint preparation, weld defects and safety.', 'SSD_ARC_WELDING', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_022_M04_S01', 'Lathe operations', '1', 'Lathe operations: Material-removal operations performed on a lathe in which a workpiece rotates while a cutting tool removes material. In Machining, the focus is on turning, facing, tapering, threading, boring, cutting speed, feed, depth of cut and tool geometry.', 'SSD_LATHE_OPERATIONS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_022_M05_S01', 'Electrical discharge machining', '1', 'Electrical discharge machining refers to a non-contact machining process that removes electrically conductive workpiece material through controlled electrical discharges in a dielectric medium. In Non-traditional Machining, the focus is on electrode/workpiece gap, spark energy, dielectric, material removal rate, surface finish and tool wear.', 'SSD_ELECTRICAL_DISCHARGE_MACHINING', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_023_M01_S01', 'Von Mises', '1', 'Von Mises refers to the von Mises yield criterion predicts yielding of ductile isotropic materials from the distortion-energy component of the stress state. In Failure Theories, the focus is on equivalent von Mises stress, multiaxial stress states, yield strength comparison and ductile-metal applicability.', 'SSD_VON_MISES', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_023_M02_S01', 'Goodman diagram', '1', 'Goodman diagram refers to a fatigue-design diagram relating alternating stress and mean stress to an endurance-strength criterion, commonly using a linear Goodman relation. In Fatigue Design, the focus is on mean stress, alternating stress, endurance strength, ultimate strength and safety factors.', 'SSD_GOODMAN_DIAGRAM', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_023_M03_S01', 'Shaft and key design', '1', 'Shaft and key design: Design of rotating shafts and keys to transmit torque while satisfying strength, stiffness, fatigue and connection requirements. In Shafts & Keys, the focus is on torsional/bending stresses, diameter, key dimensions, stress concentrations, deflection and torque transmission.', 'SSD_SHAFT_AND_KEY_DESIGN', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_023_M04_S01', 'Journal bearings', '1', 'Journal bearings: Bearings that support a rotating shaft through sliding contact, commonly separated by a lubricating film under hydrodynamic or related regimes. In Springs & Bearings, the focus is on bearing pressure, viscosity, clearance, Sommerfeld-type parameters, lubrication regime, friction and heat generation.', 'SSD_JOURNAL_BEARINGS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_023_M05_S01', 'Gear design fundamentals', '1', 'Gear design fundamentals: Principles used to select and proportion gears for transmitting motion and torque while satisfying strength, wear, accuracy and service-life requirements. In Gears, the focus is on gear geometry, module/diametral pitch, tooth forces, bending/contact stress, ratios and failure modes.', 'SSD_GEAR_DESIGN_FUNDAMENTALS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_024_M01_S01', 'Laplace transforms', '1', 'Laplace transforms refers to an integral transform that maps suitable time-domain functions to an algebraic function of a complex variable and is widely used to analyze linear dynamic systems. In System Modeling, the focus is on transform definition, properties, inverse transform, poles/zeros and differential-equation solution.', 'SSD_LAPLACE_TRANSFORMS', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_024_M02_S01', 'Time-domain response', '1', 'Time-domain response refers to the temporal output behaviour of a dynamic system following an input, disturbance or initial condition. In Time Domain Analysis, the focus is on transient and steady-state response, rise time, settling time, overshoot, damping and natural frequency.', 'SSD_TIME_DOMAIN_RESPONSE', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_024_M03_S01', 'Routh-Hurwitz and Nyquist criteria', '1', 'Routh-Hurwitz and Nyquist criteria: Frequency- or polynomial-domain stability-analysis methods used to determine whether a feedback system has unstable poles or encirclements associated with closed-loop instability. In Stability, the focus is on routh array, characteristic polynomial, Nyquist plot, encirclement criterion and open-loop/closed-loop relationships.', 'SSD_ROUTH_HURWITZ_AND_NYQUIST_CRITERIA', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_024_M04_S01', 'Bode plot', '1', 'Bode plot refers to a logarithmic magnitude-and-phase representation of a system''s frequency response as a function of frequency. In Frequency Domain Analysis, the focus is on magnitude in decibels, phase, corner frequencies, asymptotic construction and gain/phase margins.', 'SSD_BODE_PLOT', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_024_M05_S01', 'PID control', '1', 'PID control: Feedback control using proportional, integral, and derivative actions to regulate a process variable based on the control error. In Controller Design, the focus is on concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules.', 'SSD_PID_CONTROL', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '1.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M1_S1', 'agents and environments', '1', 'agents and environments: agents and environments in Artificial Intelligence concerns the interaction between an intelligent agent and the environment through percepts, actions, state transitions, and performance measures. In Intelligent Agents, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of agents and environments within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Intelligent Agents module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M1_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M1_S2', 'rational action', '2', 'rational action: rational action in Artificial Intelligence concerns the selection of actions that maximize expected performance given the agent''s percept history, knowledge, and available actions. In Intelligent Agents, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of rational action within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Intelligent Agents module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M1_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M1_S3', 'agent architectures', '3', 'agent architectures: agent architectures in Artificial Intelligence concerns the computational organization of sensing, internal state, reasoning, learning, and action used to implement an intelligent agent. In Intelligent Agents, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of agent architectures within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Intelligent Agents module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M1_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M1_S4', 'utility and performance measures', '4', 'utility and performance measures: utility and performance measures in Artificial Intelligence concerns formal measures used to represent preferences or assess how effectively an agent achieves its specified objectives. In Intelligent Agents, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of utility and performance measures within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Intelligent Agents module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M1_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M2_S1', 'state-space formulation', '1', 'state-space formulation: state-space formulation in Artificial Intelligence concerns the representation of a problem as states, actions or operators, an initial state, goal conditions, and transition relationships. In Problem Solving and Search, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of state-space formulation within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Problem Solving and Search module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M2_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M2_S2', 'uninformed search', '2', 'uninformed search: uninformed search in Artificial Intelligence concerns search strategies that use problem structure such as depth, cost, or breadth without heuristic estimates of distance to a goal. In Problem Solving and Search, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of uninformed search within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Problem Solving and Search module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M2_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M2_S3', 'heuristic search', '3', 'heuristic search: heuristic search in Artificial Intelligence concerns search strategies that use an estimate of remaining cost or distance to guide exploration toward promising states. In Problem Solving and Search, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of heuristic search within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Problem Solving and Search module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M2_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M2_S4', 'local search', '4', 'local search: local search in Artificial Intelligence concerns iterative optimization or search methods that maintain one or a small number of candidate states and improve them using neighbourhood information. In Problem Solving and Search, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of local search within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Problem Solving and Search module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M2_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M2_S5', 'adversarial search', '5', 'adversarial search: adversarial search in Artificial Intelligence concerns search for decision-making in competitive environments where an agent must account for an opposing agent''s actions, typically using minimax-style reasoning. In Problem Solving and Search, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of adversarial search within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Problem Solving and Search module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M2_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M3_S1', 'propositional logic', '1', 'propositional logic: propositional logic in Artificial Intelligence concerns a formal logic in which propositions are represented by Boolean-valued symbols and combined with logical connectives to support deduction. In Knowledge Representation and Reasoning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of propositional logic within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Knowledge Representation and Reasoning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M3_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M3_S2', 'first-order logic', '2', 'first-order logic: first-order logic in Artificial Intelligence concerns a predicate logic that represents objects, properties, and relations using predicates, variables, quantifiers, and logical connectives. In Knowledge Representation and Reasoning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of first-order logic within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Knowledge Representation and Reasoning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M3_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M3_S3', 'ontologies', '3', 'ontologies: ontologies in Artificial Intelligence concerns formal specifications of concepts, relationships, constraints, and axioms within a domain for shared semantic representation and automated reasoning. In Knowledge Representation and Reasoning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of ontologies within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Knowledge Representation and Reasoning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M3_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M3_S4', 'knowledge graphs', '4', 'knowledge graphs: knowledge graphs in Artificial Intelligence concerns graph-based representations in which entities and relations are represented as nodes and edges to support semantic integration, querying, and inference. In Knowledge Representation and Reasoning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of knowledge graphs within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Knowledge Representation and Reasoning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M3_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M3_S5', 'inference', '5', 'inference: inference in Artificial Intelligence concerns the derivation of conclusions from represented facts, rules, models, or observations using a specified reasoning procedure. In Knowledge Representation and Reasoning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of inference within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Knowledge Representation and Reasoning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M3_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M3_S6', 'reasoning under uncertainty', '6', 'reasoning under uncertainty: reasoning under uncertainty in Artificial Intelligence concerns methods for representing incomplete or uncertain knowledge and deriving conclusions when truth values, probabilities, or evidence are not fully determined. In Knowledge Representation and Reasoning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of reasoning under uncertainty within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Knowledge Representation and Reasoning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M3_S6', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M4_S1', 'classical planning', '1', 'classical planning: Planning in which actions have known preconditions and effects and a plan is a sequence of actions that achieves specified goals. In Planning and Decision Making, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of classical planning within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Planning and Decision Making module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M4_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M4_S2', 'partial-order planning', '2', 'partial-order planning: Planning that represents only the ordering constraints required between actions, allowing independent actions to remain unordered. In Planning and Decision Making, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of partial-order planning within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Planning and Decision Making module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M4_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M4_S3', 'probabilistic decision making', '3', 'probabilistic decision making: Choosing actions by comparing their expected outcomes when states, observations, or outcomes are uncertain. In Planning and Decision Making, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of probabilistic decision making within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Planning and Decision Making module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M4_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M4_S4', 'Markov decision processes', '4', 'Markov decision processes refers to a model of sequential decisions in which the next state depends on the current state and chosen action. In Planning and Decision Making, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of Markov decision processes within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Planning and Decision Making module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M4_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M4_S5', 'sequential decision making', '5', 'sequential decision making: Selecting a sequence of actions over time while accounting for future states, rewards, and uncertainty. In Planning and Decision Making, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of sequential decision making within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Planning and Decision Making module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M4_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M5_S1', 'learning paradigms', '1', 'learning paradigms: Major ways an AI system learns from data or interaction, including supervised, unsupervised, self-supervised, and reinforcement learning. In Machine Learning Foundations, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of learning paradigms within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Machine Learning Foundations module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M5_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M5_S2', 'hypothesis spaces', '2', 'hypothesis spaces refers to the set of candidate functions or models that a learning algorithm can select from. In Machine Learning Foundations, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of hypothesis spaces within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Machine Learning Foundations module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M5_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M5_S3', 'feature representations', '3', 'feature representations: Ways of encoding raw data as measurable variables that an AI model can use for learning or prediction. In Machine Learning Foundations, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of feature representations within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Machine Learning Foundations module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M5_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M5_S4', 'generalization', '4', 'generalization refers to the ability of a trained model to perform well on previously unseen data. In Machine Learning Foundations, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of generalization within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Machine Learning Foundations module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M5_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M5_S5', 'bias-variance', '5', 'bias-variance refers to the trade-off between systematic model error and sensitivity to training-data variation. In Machine Learning Foundations, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of bias-variance within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Machine Learning Foundations module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M5_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M5_S6', 'learning pipelines', '6', 'learning pipelines: learning pipelines in Artificial Intelligence concerns ordered data, training, validation, packaging, and deployment stages that make machine-learning workflows reproducible and operational. In Machine Learning Foundations, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of learning pipelines within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Machine Learning Foundations module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M5_S6', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M6_S1', 'text representation', '1', 'text representation: Encoding words, tokens, or documents in forms that AI models can process computationally. In Natural Language Processing, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of text representation within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Natural Language Processing module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M6_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M6_S2', 'language models', '2', 'language models: Models that assign probabilities to sequences of language and use them to predict or generate text. In Natural Language Processing, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of language models within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Natural Language Processing module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M6_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M6_S3', 'sequence modelling', '3', 'sequence modelling: Modelling ordered observations or events so that dependencies across sequence positions can be learned and used for prediction or classification. In Natural Language Processing, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of sequence modelling within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Natural Language Processing module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M6_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M6_S4', 'parsing', '4', 'parsing: Analysing the grammatical or structural organisation of a sentence or other language sequence. In Natural Language Processing, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of parsing within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Natural Language Processing module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M6_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M6_S5', 'information extraction', '5', 'information extraction: Automatically identifying structured facts, entities, relations, or events from unstructured text. In Natural Language Processing, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of information extraction within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Natural Language Processing module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M6_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M6_S6', 'evaluation', '6', 'evaluation: Systematic assessment of an AI model or system using task-appropriate performance measures, test data, and error analysis. In Natural Language Processing, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of evaluation within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Natural Language Processing module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M6_S6', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M7_S1', 'image formation', '1', 'image formation refers to the process by which a scene is projected and recorded as an image through an imaging system. In Computer Vision and Perception, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of image formation within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Computer Vision and Perception module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M7_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M7_S2', 'feature extraction', '2', 'feature extraction: Computing informative image patterns such as edges, textures, shapes, or learned representations. In Computer Vision and Perception, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of feature extraction within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Computer Vision and Perception module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M7_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M7_S3', 'classification', '3', 'classification: Assigning an input image or instance to one or more predefined categories. In Computer Vision and Perception, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of classification within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Computer Vision and Perception module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M7_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M7_S4', 'object detection', '4', 'object detection: Locating objects in an image and assigning class labels to the detected objects. In Computer Vision and Perception, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of object detection within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Computer Vision and Perception module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M7_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M7_S5', 'segmentation', '5', 'segmentation: Assigning labels to image pixels or regions to separate objects or semantic areas. In Computer Vision and Perception, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of segmentation within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Computer Vision and Perception module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M7_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M7_S6', 'evaluation', '6', 'evaluation: Systematic assessment of an AI model or system using task-appropriate performance measures, test data, and error analysis. In Computer Vision and Perception, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of evaluation within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the Natural Language Processing module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M7_S6', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M8_S1', 'AI system architecture', '1', 'AI system architecture refers to the organization of models, data, software, computing resources, interfaces, and supporting services that together implement an AI system. In AI Systems, Safety and Ethics, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of AI system architecture within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the AI Systems, Safety and Ethics module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M8_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M8_S2', 'robustness', '2', 'robustness refers to the ability of an AI system to maintain acceptable performance under disturbances, uncertainty, or input variation. In AI Systems, Safety and Ethics, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of robustness within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the AI Systems, Safety and Ethics module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M8_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M8_S3', 'interpretability', '3', 'interpretability refers to the extent to which a model''s predictions or internal reasoning can be understood by people. In AI Systems, Safety and Ethics, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of interpretability within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the AI Systems, Safety and Ethics module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M8_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M8_S4', 'fairness', '4', 'fairness refers to the use of defined criteria to assess and reduce unjustified differences in model outcomes across groups. In AI Systems, Safety and Ethics, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of fairness within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the AI Systems, Safety and Ethics module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M8_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M8_S5', 'privacy', '5', 'privacy: Protection of personal or sensitive information during AI data collection, processing, storage, and use. In AI Systems, Safety and Ethics, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of privacy within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the AI Systems, Safety and Ethics module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M8_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_025_M8_S6', 'safety and governance', '6', 'safety and governance: safety and governance in Artificial Intelligence concerns legal rules, institutional mechanisms, duties, procedures, and compliance considerations governing safety and governance. In AI Systems, Safety and Ethics, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of safety and governance within Artificial Intelligence, particularly where the AI Systems, Safety and Ethics module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_025_M8_S6', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M1_S1', 'supervised learning', '1', 'supervised learning: Supervised learning learns a mapping from inputs to labelled outputs using observed training examples. In Learning Paradigms, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of supervised learning within Machine Learning, particularly where the Learning Paradigms module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M1_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M1_S2', 'unsupervised learning', '2', 'unsupervised learning: Unsupervised learning infers structure or representations from data without target labels, including clustering and dimensionality-reduction tasks. In Learning Paradigms, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of unsupervised learning within Machine Learning, particularly where the Learning Paradigms module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M1_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M1_S3', 'semi-supervised learning', '3', 'semi-supervised learning: Semi-supervised learning combines labelled and unlabelled observations to improve learning when labelled data are limited. In Learning Paradigms, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of semi-supervised learning within Machine Learning, particularly where the Learning Paradigms module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M1_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M1_S4', 'self-supervised learning', '4', 'self-supervised learning: Self-supervised learning constructs learning signals from the data itself, typically by predicting withheld, transformed, or related information. In Learning Paradigms, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of self-supervised learning within Machine Learning, particularly where the Learning Paradigms module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M1_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M1_S5', 'reinforcement learning', '5', 'reinforcement learning: Reinforcement learning models sequential decision making in which an agent learns a policy from interactions with an environment and feedback in the form of rewards or costs. In Learning Paradigms, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of reinforcement learning within Machine Learning, particularly where the Learning Paradigms module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M1_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M2_S1', 'data cleaning', '1', 'data cleaning: Data cleaning identifies and corrects or documents errors, inconsistencies, duplicates, invalid values, and other quality problems before analysis or modelling. In Data Preparation and Feature Engineering, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of data cleaning within Machine Learning, particularly where the Data Preparation and Feature Engineering module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M2_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M2_S2', 'missing values', '2', 'missing values: Missing-value handling comprises methods for diagnosing missingness and deciding whether to remove, retain, or impute incomplete observations. In Data Preparation and Feature Engineering, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of missing values within Machine Learning, particularly where the Data Preparation and Feature Engineering module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M2_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M2_S3', 'categorical encoding', '3', 'categorical encoding: Categorical encoding represents non-numeric categories using numerical or structured representations suitable for statistical or machine-learning models. In Data Preparation and Feature Engineering, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of categorical encoding within Machine Learning, particularly where the Data Preparation and Feature Engineering module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M2_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M2_S4', 'scaling', '4', 'scaling: Transforming numerical features to comparable ranges so that model training is not dominated by variable magnitude. In Data Preparation and Feature Engineering, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of scaling within Machine Learning, particularly where the Data Preparation and Feature Engineering module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M2_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M2_S5', 'feature selection', '5', 'feature selection: Choosing a subset of input features that preserves useful predictive information while reducing redundancy, noise, or model complexity. In Data Preparation and Feature Engineering, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of feature selection within Machine Learning, particularly where the Data Preparation and Feature Engineering module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M2_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M2_S6', 'leakage control', '6', 'leakage control: Preventing information from the target, future observations, or evaluation data from entering model training in a way that produces overly optimistic results. In Data Preparation and Feature Engineering, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of leakage control within Machine Learning, particularly where the Data Preparation and Feature Engineering module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M2_S6', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M3_S1', 'linear regression', '1', 'linear regression refers to a regression model that represents the target as a linear function of the input features. In Regression and Classification, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of linear regression within Machine Learning, particularly where the Regression and Classification module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M3_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M3_S2', 'logistic regression', '2', 'logistic regression refers to a probabilistic classification model that relates features to class probability through the logistic function. In Regression and Classification, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of logistic regression within Machine Learning, particularly where the Regression and Classification module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M3_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M3_S3', 'regularization', '3', 'regularization: Adding a penalty or constraint to limit model complexity and reduce overfitting. In Regression and Classification, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of regularization within Machine Learning, particularly where the Regression and Classification module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M3_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M3_S4', 'decision trees', '4', 'decision trees: Models that make predictions by recursively splitting data using feature-based decision rules. In Regression and Classification, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of decision trees within Machine Learning, particularly where the Regression and Classification module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M3_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M3_S5', 'ensemble methods', '5', 'ensemble methods: Methods that combine predictions from multiple models to improve accuracy, stability, or robustness. In Regression and Classification, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of ensemble methods within Machine Learning, particularly where the Regression and Classification module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M3_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M3_S6', 'support vector machines', '6', 'support vector machines: Supervised learning models that construct decision boundaries using support vectors and, when required, kernel functions to represent nonlinear relationships. In Regression and Classification, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of support vector machines within Machine Learning, particularly where the Regression and Classification module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M3_S6', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M4_S1', 'probability models', '1', 'probability models: Mathematical models that represent uncertainty in data, variables, and relationships using probability distributions. In Probabilistic and Bayesian Learning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of probability models within Machine Learning, particularly where the Probabilistic and Bayesian Learning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M4_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M4_S2', 'Bayes rule', '2', 'Bayes rule refers to a rule for updating the probability of a hypothesis using observed evidence. In Probabilistic and Bayesian Learning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of Bayes rule within Machine Learning, particularly where the Probabilistic and Bayesian Learning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M4_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M4_S3', 'naive Bayes', '3', 'naive Bayes refers to a Bayesian classifier that assumes conditional independence among features given the class. In Probabilistic and Bayesian Learning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of naive Bayes within Machine Learning, particularly where the Probabilistic and Bayesian Learning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M4_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M4_S4', 'graphical models', '4', 'graphical models: Probabilistic models that represent conditional dependencies between variables using a graph. In Probabilistic and Bayesian Learning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of graphical models within Machine Learning, particularly where the Probabilistic and Bayesian Learning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M4_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M4_S5', 'maximum likelihood', '5', 'maximum likelihood: Estimating model parameters by choosing values that make the observed data most probable. In Probabilistic and Bayesian Learning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of maximum likelihood within Machine Learning, particularly where the Probabilistic and Bayesian Learning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M4_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M4_S6', 'Bayesian inference', '6', 'Bayesian inference: Updating prior beliefs about model parameters using observed data to obtain a posterior distribution. In Probabilistic and Bayesian Learning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of Bayesian inference within Machine Learning, particularly where the Probabilistic and Bayesian Learning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M4_S6', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M5_S1', 'clustering', '1', 'clustering: Grouping observations into internally similar sets without using predefined class labels. In Unsupervised Learning and Representation, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of clustering within Machine Learning, particularly where the Unsupervised Learning and Representation module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M5_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M5_S2', 'dimensionality reduction', '2', 'dimensionality reduction: Representing high-dimensional data with fewer variables while retaining important structure or information. In Unsupervised Learning and Representation, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of dimensionality reduction within Machine Learning, particularly where the Unsupervised Learning and Representation module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M5_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M5_S3', 'principal component analysis', '3', 'principal component analysis refers to a dimensionality-reduction method that transforms correlated variables into orthogonal principal components ordered by explained variance. In Unsupervised Learning and Representation, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of principal component analysis within Machine Learning, particularly where the Unsupervised Learning and Representation module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M5_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M5_S4', 'mixture models', '4', 'mixture models: Probabilistic models that represent data as arising from a combination of component distributions. In Unsupervised Learning and Representation, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of mixture models within Machine Learning, particularly where the Unsupervised Learning and Representation module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M5_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M5_S5', 'manifold learning', '5', 'manifold learning: Nonlinear dimensionality-reduction methods that model data as lying near a lower-dimensional manifold. In Unsupervised Learning and Representation, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of manifold learning within Machine Learning, particularly where the Unsupervised Learning and Representation module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M5_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M6_S1', 'perceptrons', '1', 'perceptrons: Single-layer threshold-based units that form the basic computational model of a linear classifier. In Neural Networks and Deep Learning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of perceptrons within Machine Learning, particularly where the Neural Networks and Deep Learning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M6_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M6_S2', 'multilayer networks', '2', 'multilayer networks: Neural networks containing successive layers of interconnected units that learn nonlinear mappings. In Neural Networks and Deep Learning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of multilayer networks within Machine Learning, particularly where the Neural Networks and Deep Learning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M6_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M6_S3', 'backpropagation', '3', 'backpropagation refers to an algorithm that computes gradients through a neural network so its parameters can be updated during training. In Neural Networks and Deep Learning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of backpropagation within Machine Learning, particularly where the Neural Networks and Deep Learning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M6_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M6_S4', 'convolutional networks', '4', 'convolutional networks: Neural networks using convolutional filters to learn local spatial or temporal patterns. In Neural Networks and Deep Learning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of convolutional networks within Machine Learning, particularly where the Neural Networks and Deep Learning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M6_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M6_S5', 'sequence models', '5', 'sequence models: Models designed to learn dependencies among ordered observations such as words, signals, or time-series values. In Neural Networks and Deep Learning, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of sequence models within Machine Learning, particularly where the Neural Networks and Deep Learning module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M6_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M6_S6', 'optimization', '6', 'optimization: Selection of decision variables or operating conditions to maximize or minimize an objective subject to specified constraints; the objective and constraints depend on the application domain. In Neural Networks and Deep Learning, the focus is on concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M6_S6', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M7_S1', 'cross-validation', '1', 'cross-validation: Cross-validation repeatedly partitions available data into training and validation subsets to estimate model performance and support model selection. In Model Evaluation and Deployment, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of cross-validation within Machine Learning, particularly where the Model Evaluation and Deployment module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M7_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M7_S2', 'calibration', '2', 'calibration: Adjusting predicted probabilities so that they correspond appropriately to observed outcome frequencies; in ML this concerns probabilistic prediction calibration, not instrument adjustment. In Model Evaluation and Deployment, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of calibration within Machine Learning, particularly where the Model Evaluation and Deployment module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M7_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M7_S3', 'imbalanced data', '3', 'imbalanced data refers to a dataset in which some classes or outcomes occur much less often than others. In Model Evaluation and Deployment, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of imbalanced data within Machine Learning, particularly where the Model Evaluation and Deployment module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M7_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M7_S4', 'hyperparameter selection', '4', 'hyperparameter selection: Choosing model settings that are not learned directly from the training data, typically using validation procedures or cross-validation. In Model Evaluation and Deployment, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of hyperparameter selection within Machine Learning, particularly where the Model Evaluation and Deployment module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M7_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M7_S5', 'model monitoring', '5', 'model monitoring: Tracking a deployed model''s inputs, outputs, performance, and operating conditions to detect degradation or drift. In Model Evaluation and Deployment, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of model monitoring within Machine Learning, particularly where the Model Evaluation and Deployment module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M7_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_026_M7_S6', 'reproducibility', '6', 'reproducibility refers to the ability to obtain consistent results when the same analysis, data, methods, and documented computational steps are repeated. In Model Evaluation and Deployment, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of reproducibility within Machine Learning, particularly where the Model Evaluation and Deployment module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_026_M7_S6', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M1_S1', 'system models', '1', 'system models: Abstract assumptions about processes, communication, timing, failures, and resources in a distributed system. In Distributed System Models, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of system models within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed System Models module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M1_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M1_S2', 'communication models', '2', 'communication models: Assumptions about how distributed processes exchange messages, including timing, ordering, and delivery guarantees. In Distributed System Models, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of communication models within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed System Models module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M1_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M1_S3', 'time and ordering', '3', 'time and ordering: Methods for reasoning about event order when distributed processes do not share a perfectly synchronised clock. In Distributed System Models, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of time and ordering within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed System Models module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M1_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M1_S4', 'failure models', '4', 'failure models: Formal assumptions about how components or processes may fail in a distributed system, such as crash, omission, timing, or Byzantine failures. In Distributed System Models, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of failure models within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed System Models module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M1_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M1_S5', 'scalability', '5', 'scalability refers to the ability of a distributed system to maintain acceptable performance as workload, data, or nodes increase. In Distributed System Models, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of scalability within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed System Models module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M1_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M2_S1', 'Remote Procedure Call (RPC)', '1', 'Remote Procedure Call (RPC) refers to a communication mechanism that lets a program invoke an operation on a remote process using a call-like interface. In Communication and Coordination, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of RPC within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Communication and Coordination module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M2_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M2_S2', 'messaging', '2', 'messaging: Exchange of discrete messages between distributed components to coordinate work or transfer data. In Communication and Coordination, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of messaging within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Communication and Coordination module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M2_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M2_S3', 'multicast', '3', 'multicast: Sending one message to multiple intended recipients in a distributed network. In Communication and Coordination, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of multicast within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Communication and Coordination module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M2_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M2_S4', 'logical clocks', '4', 'logical clocks: Logical mechanisms for ordering distributed events without relying on synchronised physical clocks. In Communication and Coordination, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of logical clocks within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Communication and Coordination module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M2_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M2_S5', 'leader election', '5', 'leader election refers to a protocol for selecting one distributed process to coordinate activities or make designated decisions. In Communication and Coordination, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of leader election within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Communication and Coordination module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M2_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M2_S6', 'distributed coordination', '6', 'distributed coordination: Protocols that allow independent processes to reach compatible decisions or organise shared work. In Communication and Coordination, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of distributed coordination within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Communication and Coordination module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M2_S6', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M3_S1', 'primary-backup replication', '1', 'primary-backup replication: Replication in which a primary processes updates and backups maintain copies for continuity after failure. In Replication and Consistency, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of primary-backup replication within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Replication and Consistency module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M3_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M3_S2', 'quorum systems', '2', 'quorum systems: Sets of replicas whose agreement or participation is required for an operation to proceed safely. In Replication and Consistency, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of quorum systems within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Replication and Consistency module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M3_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M3_S3', 'consistency models', '3', 'consistency models: Rules defining what values and operation orders clients may observe from replicated data. In Replication and Consistency, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of consistency models within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Replication and Consistency module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M3_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M3_S4', 'consensus', '4', 'consensus refers to a distributed protocol that makes non-faulty processes agree on one value despite specified failures. In Replication and Consistency, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of consensus within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Replication and Consistency module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M3_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M3_S5', 'conflict resolution', '5', 'conflict resolution: Rules for reconciling concurrent or incompatible updates to shared distributed state. In Replication and Consistency, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of conflict resolution within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Replication and Consistency module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M3_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M4_S1', 'atomic commit', '1', 'atomic commit refers to a protocol ensuring that a distributed transaction is either committed by all required participants or aborted. In Distributed Transactions, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of atomic commit within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed Transactions module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M4_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M4_S2', 'two-phase commit', '2', 'two-phase commit refers to a distributed commit protocol using prepare and commit phases to coordinate transaction outcome. In Distributed Transactions, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of two-phase commit within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed Transactions module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M4_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M4_S3', 'distributed concurrency control', '3', 'distributed concurrency control: Coordination mechanisms that keep concurrent operations on distributed data consistent while allowing appropriate parallel execution. In Distributed Transactions, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of distributed concurrency control within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed Transactions module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M4_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M4_S4', 'serializability', '4', 'serializability refers to the property that concurrent transaction execution has an effect equivalent to some serial order. In Distributed Transactions, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of serializability within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed Transactions module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M4_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M4_S5', 'recovery', '5', 'recovery: Restoring a distributed system or transaction to a correct state after a failure, using mechanisms such as logging, checkpoints, rollback, or replay. In Distributed Transactions, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of recovery within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed Transactions module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M4_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M5_S1', 'partitioning', '1', 'partitioning: Dividing data or workload across nodes so that storage and processing can be distributed. In Distributed Storage, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of partitioning within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed Storage module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M5_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M5_S2', 'distributed hash tables', '2', 'distributed hash tables: Distributed data structures that map keys to responsible nodes for scalable lookup. In Distributed Storage, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of distributed hash tables within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed Storage module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M5_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M5_S3', 'distributed file systems', '3', 'distributed file systems: File systems that store and manage files across multiple networked machines. In Distributed Storage, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of distributed file systems within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed Storage module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M5_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M5_S4', 'object storage', '4', 'object storage refers to a storage architecture in which data are managed as objects containing payload data, metadata, and a unique identifier within a logical namespace. In Distributed Storage, the focus is on concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M5_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M5_S5', 'metadata management', '5', 'metadata management: Maintaining information about distributed files, objects, nodes, locations, and system state. In Distributed Storage, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of metadata management within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed Storage module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M5_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M6_S1', 'failure detection', '1', 'failure detection: Identifying components that are suspected to have failed, typically from timeouts, heartbeats, acknowledgements, or other observations. In Fault Tolerance and Recovery, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of failure detection within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Fault Tolerance and Recovery module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M6_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M6_S2', 'redundancy', '2', 'redundancy: Provision of duplicate or alternative components, paths, or resources so that loss or failure of one element does not necessarily cause loss of required service. In Fault Tolerance and Recovery, the focus is on concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M6_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M6_S3', 'checkpointing', '3', 'checkpointing: Saving recoverable system state so computation can resume after a failure. In Fault Tolerance and Recovery, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of checkpointing within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Fault Tolerance and Recovery module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M6_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M6_S4', 'recovery protocols', '4', 'recovery protocols: Protocols that coordinate restoration of consistent system state after failures, including rollback, replay, checkpointing, or state reconstruction. In Fault Tolerance and Recovery, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of recovery protocols within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Fault Tolerance and Recovery module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M6_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M6_S5', 'Byzantine failures', '5', 'Byzantine failures: Failures in which a distributed component may behave arbitrarily or inconsistently, including sending conflicting or misleading information. In Fault Tolerance and Recovery, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of Byzantine failures within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Fault Tolerance and Recovery module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M6_S5', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M7_S1', 'availability', '1', 'availability refers to the ability of a distributed service to remain accessible and responsive when components fail. In Distributed System Design, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of availability within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed System Design module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M7_S1', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M7_S2', 'partition tolerance', '2', 'partition tolerance refers to the ability to continue operating when network partitions prevent some nodes from communicating. In Distributed System Design, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of partition tolerance within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed System Design module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M7_S2', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M7_S3', 'load balancing', '3', 'load balancing: Distribution of computational, network, or service workload across available resources to improve utilization, throughput, latency, or availability. In Distributed System Design, the focus is on concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M7_S3', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M7_S4', 'observability', '4', 'observability refers to the ability to infer distributed-system behaviour from logs, metrics, traces, and other telemetry. In Distributed System Design, the focus is on the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of observability within Distributed Systems, particularly where the Distributed System Design module establishes its technical context.', 'SSD_COURSE_027_M7_S4', 'Semantically_Audited', 'Active', '4.0'), ('SUB_COURSE_027_M7_S5', 'performance trade-offs', '5', 'performance trade-offs: Design choices that balance latency, throughput, consistency, availability, resource use, and other system objectives. In Distributed System Design, the focus is on 