ror, propagation, uncertainty and error detection.', 'Measurement quality; uncertainty; repeatability; error propagation.', 'Surveying error analysis distinguishes systematic effects, random variation and blunders and applies appropriate checks, corrections and uncertainty assessment.', 'Measurement; uncertainty; Measurement quality; repeatability; error propagation; Surveying & Geomatics', 'Active'), ('KCR_000081', 'Benchmarks', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Surveying & Geomatics', 'Technical Concept', 'Reference points with known or established elevations used to control vertical surveying and transfer elevation information.', 'Permanent/temporary benchmarks, datum, reduced levels, levelling networks and monumentation.', 'Reference frames; traceability; control; consistency.', 'Benchmarks provide stable vertical references from which elevations can be measured or transferred within a defined datum and control network.', 'Levelling; geodetic datum; Reference frames; traceability; control; consistency', 'Active'), ('KCR_000082', 'Angular measurement', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Surveying & Geomatics', 'Technical Concept', 'Determination of horizontal or vertical angles between survey lines or directions using appropriate angular-measurement instruments.', 'Theodolites/total stations, centering, face observations, repetition, direction measurement and error control.', 'Geometric reference; precision; redundancy; instrument calibration.', 'Survey angular measurement determines directions or angles relative to a defined reference and uses observation procedures to reduce instrumental and observational error.', 'Survey instruments; measurement errors; Geometric reference; precision; redundancy; instrument calibration', 'Active'), ('KCR_000083', 'Horizontal and vertical curves', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Surveying & Geomatics', 'Technical Concept', 'Geometric transition elements used to connect roadway alignments while controlling changes in direction and grade.', 'S