umptions; solvability depends strongly on geometry and boundary conditions.', 'Momentum conservation; viscosity; continuity', 'Active'), ('KCR_000092', 'Boundary layers', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Fluid Mechanics & Machinery; Fluid Flow and Heat Transfer', 'Technical Concept', 'Thin regions adjacent to solid surfaces in which viscous effects produce strong velocity gradients and influence momentum, heat, or mass transfer.', 'Concept-level scope: the defining mechanism, properties, constraints, and application criteria; curricular context is recorded in Concept_Category and Typical_Modules.', 'Defining mechanism/properties; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria for Boundary layers.', 'Boundary-layer theory exploits the thinness of near-wall viscous regions to simplify high-Reynolds-number flows and predict shear and separation behaviour.', 'Reynolds number; viscosity; Defining mechanism/properties; governing conditions; assumptions and limitations; application/performance criteria for Boundary layers', 'Active'), ('KCR_000093', 'Pelton and Francis turbines', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Fluid Mechanics & Machinery', 'Technical Concept', 'Hydraulic turbine types represented by Pelton impulse turbines and Francis reaction turbines for converting water energy into shaft power.', 'Pelton jet/bucket interaction; Francis runner, pressure change, head, flow rate, efficiency and operating range.', 'Energy conversion; hydraulic efficiency; flow control; mechanical power.', 'Pelton turbines extract energy primarily from high-velocity jets and are suited to high-head applications; Francis turbines are reaction turbines commonly used over moderate head/flow ranges.', 'Hydraulic turbines; energy equation; Energy conversion; hydraulic efficiency; flow control; mechanical power', 'Active'), ('KCR_000094', 'Centrifugal pumps', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Fluid Mechanics & Machinery; Hydraulics and Hydraulic Engineering', 'Technical C