g mechanical energy-storage elements that reduce cyclic speed fluctuations by storing and releasing kinetic energy.', 'Energy fluctuation, moment of inertia, coefficient of speed fluctuation and angular velocity.', 'Energy storage; inertia; speed regulation.', 'A flywheel stores kinetic energy proportional to rotational inertia and the square of angular speed and smooths periodic speed variations.', 'Rotational dynamics; energy storage; inertia; speed regulation; Dynamics of Machines', 'Active'), ('KCR_000106', 'Static and dynamic balancing', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Dynamics of Machines', 'Technical Concept', 'Procedures for reducing unbalanced forces and moments in rotating or reciprocating machinery.', 'Mass distribution, centrifugal forces, static balance, couple balance, correction planes and balancing procedures.', 'Force balance; moment balance; vibration reduction.', 'Static balancing addresses resultant unbalanced force, while dynamic balancing also accounts for the resultant unbalanced couple and generally requires correction in multiple planes.', 'Rotating machinery; vibration; Force balance; moment balance; vibration reduction; Dynamics of Machines', 'Active'), ('KCR_000107', 'Natural frequency', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Dynamics of Machines', 'Technical Concept', 'A characteristic frequency at which a system can oscillate freely after a disturbance in the absence of sustained external excitation and damping effects.', 'Single/multi-degree systems, stiffness, mass, damping influence and mode shapes.', 'Inertia; stiffness; modal behaviour.', 'Natural frequencies arise from the system''s mass and stiffness properties; damping modifies the observed damped frequency and response.', 'Free vibration; modal analysis; Inertia; stiffness; modal behaviour; Dynamics of Machines', 'Active'), ('KCR_000108', 'Resonance', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Dynamics of Machines', 'Technical Concept', 'A condition in which forced vibration response becomes large when excitation frequency approaches an appropriate natural frequency of the system.', 'Frequency response, damping, natural frequency, amplitude and phase behaviour.', 'Dynamic amplification; frequency matching; damping.', 'Resonance results from strong dynamic response near a system''s natural frequency. Damping limits peak response, but the precise resonance condition depends on the response measure.', 'Natural frequency; forced vibration; Dynamic amplification; frequency matching; damping; Dynamics of Machines', 'Active'), ('KCR_000109', 'Governor and gyroscope principles', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Dynamics of Machines', 'Technical Concept', 'Rotational-mechanics principles represented by governors for speed regulation and gyroscopes for angular-momentum-based orientation and reaction effects.', 'Governor equilibrium/speed regulation; gyroscopic moment, precession and angular momentum.', 'Feedback/regulation; angular momentum; dynamic stability.', 'A governor mechanically senses speed-related conditions to regulate engine input, while a gyroscope exhibits orientation and reaction behaviour arising from angular momentum and precession.', 'Rotational dynamics; angular momentum; Feedback/regulation; dynamic stability; Dynamics of Machines', 'Active'), ('KCR_000110', 'Sand casting', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Manufacturing Processes', 'Method / Process', 'A metal casting process in which molten metal is poured into a mould cavity formed in compacted sand.', 'Pattern, moulding sand, gating/riser system, solidification, defects and post-casting finishing.', 'Material shaping; solidification; resource use; process quality.', 'Sand casting produces near-net-shape components by solidifying molten metal in a disposable sand mould. Quality depends on mould design, metal flow and solidification control.', 'Casting; solidification; Material shaping; resource use; process quality; Manufacturing Processes', 'Active'), ('KCR_000111', 'Forging', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Manu