, or evaluation of post-processing within CAD/CAM, particularly where the Computer-Aided Manufacturing module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of post-processing, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'post-processing; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of post-processing, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; CAD/CAM', 'Active'), ('KCR_000499', 'machining optimization', 'Engineering & Technology', 'CAD/CAM', 'Technical Concept', 'Selecting tool paths and process parameters to balance productivity, surface quality, tool life, and machining constraints.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of machining optimization within CAD/CAM, particularly where the Computer-Aided Manufacturing module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of machining optimization, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Selecting tool paths and process parameters to balance productivity, surface quality, tool life, and machining constraints. Within Computer-Aided Manufacturing, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of machining optimization within CAD/CAM, particularly where the Computer-Aided Manufacturing module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of machining optimization, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'machining optimization; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of machining optimization, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; CAD/CAM', 'Active'), ('KCR_000500', 'associativity', 'Engineering & Technology', 'CAD/CAM', 'Technical Concept', 'Maintaining links so changes to related CAD geometry, features, drawings, or manufacturing data can propagate consistently.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of associativity within CAD/CAM, particularly where the CAD/CAM Integration and Product Data module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of associativity, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Maintaining links so changes to related CAD geometry, features, drawings, or manufacturing data can propagate consistently. Within CAD/CAM Integration and Product Data, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of associativity within CAD/CAM, particularly where the CAD/CAM Integration and Product Data module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of associativity, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'associativity; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of associativity, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; CAD/CAM', 'Active') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO repo_kcrs (kcr_id, name, domain, concept_category, concept_type, definition, scope, core_principles, semantic_description, keywords_synonyms, status) VALUES ('KCR_000501', 'product data exchange', 'Engineering & Technology', 'CAD/CAM', 'Technical Concept', 'Transferring product geometry and engineering information between different CAD/CAM systems using defined data formats.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of product data exchange within CAD/CAM, particularly where the CAD/CAM Integration and Product Data module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of product data exchange, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Transferring product geometry and engineering information between different CAD/CAM systems using defined data formats. Within CAD/CAM Integration and Product Data, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of product data exchange within CAD/CAM, particularly where the CAD/CAM Integration and Product Data module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of product data exchange, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'product data exchange; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of product data exchange, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; CAD/CAM', 'Active'), ('KCR_000502', 'Product Lifecycle Management (PLM)', 'Engineering & Technology', 'CAD/CAM', 'Technical Concept', 'Product Lifecycle Management, the controlled management of product information and processes from design through manufacture, service, and retirem