ion; quorum systems; consistency models; consensus; conflict resolution; atomic commit; two-phase commit; distributed concurrency control; serializability; recovery; partitioning; distributed hash tables; distributed file systems; object storage; metadata management; failure detection; redundancy; checkpointing; recovery protocols; Byzantine failures; availability; partition tolerance; load balancing; observability; performance trade-offs', '', 'Curriculum-derived disciplinary scope', 'Active'), ('GR_COURSE_028', 'Course', 'Cloud Computing and Virtualization', 'IaaS; PaaS; SaaS; public/private/hybrid cloud; shared responsibility; hypervisors; virtual machines; containers; hardware virtualization; resource isolation; provisioning; autoscaling; scheduling; resource allocation; capacity planning; object storage; block storage; file storage; distributed databases; data durability; virtual networks; subnets; routing; load balancing; service discovery; network security; infrastructure as code; configuration management; orchestration; service deployment; autoscaling policies; identity and access management; encryption; isolation; resilience; backup and disaster recovery', 'Cloud scheduling, virtualization, scaling, or resource allocation does not by itself establish sustainability, equity, or need-based allocation; the application must explicitly connect allocation or capacity decisions to energy, resource, need, impact, or another sustainability consequence.', 'Curriculum-derived disciplinary scope', 'Active'), ('GR_COURSE_029', 'Course', 'Data Center Operations and Infrastructure', 'site planning; rack layout; power distribution; cooling architecture; physical security; server architectures; processors; memory; storage controllers; accelerators; hardware lifecycle; RAID; SAN; NAS; object storage; backup; data protection; topologies; switching; routing; load balancing; network virtualization; high-availability design; UPS; generators; power distribution; PUE; demand manag