perience of public services', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_16_7_1', '16.7.1', 'Proportions of positions in national and local institutions, including (a) the legislatures; (b) the public service; and (c) the judiciary, compared to national distributions, by sex, age, persons with disabilities and population groups', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_16_7_2', '16.7.2', 'Proportion of population who believe decision-making is inclusive and responsive, by sex, age, disability and population group', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_16_8_1', '16.8.1', 'Proportion of members and voting rights of developing countries in international organizations', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_16_9_1', '16.9.1', 'Proportion of children under 5 years of age whose births have been registered with a civil authority, by age', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_16_10_1', '16.10.1', 'Number of verified cases of killing, kidnapping, enforced disappearance, arbitrary detention and torture of journalists, associated media personnel, trade unionists and human rights advocates in the previous 12 months', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_16_10_2', '16.10.2', 'Number of countries that adopt and implement constitutional, statutory and/or policy guarantees for public access to information', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_16_a_1', '16.a.1', 'Existence of independent national human rights institutions in compliance with the Paris Principles', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_16_b_1', '16.b.1', 'Proportion of population reporting having personally felt discriminated against or harassed in the previous 12 months on the basis of a ground of discrimination prohibited under international human rights law', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_1_1', '17.1.1', 'Total government revenue as a proportion of GDP, by source', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_1_2', '17.1.2', 'Proportion of domestic budget funded by domestic taxes', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_2_1', '17.2.1', 'Net official development assistance, total and to least developed countries, as a proportion of the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD) Development Assistance Committee donors’ gross national income (GNI)', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_3_1', '17.3.1', 'Additional financial resources mobilized for developing countries from multiple sources', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_3_2', '17.3.2', 'Volume of remittances (in United States dollars) as a proportion of total GDP', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_4_1', '17.4.1', 'Debt service as a proportion of exports of goods, services and primary income', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_5_1', '17.5.1', 'Number of countries that adopt and implement investment promotion regimes for developing countries, including the least developed countries', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_6_1', '17.6.1', 'Fixed broadband subscriptions per 100 inhabitants, by speed', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_7_1', '17.7.1', 'Total amount of funding for developing and developed countries to promote the development, transfer, dissemination and diffusion of environmentally sound technologies', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_8_1', '17.8.1', 'Proportion of individuals using the Internet', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_9_1', '17.9.1', 'Dollar value of official development assistance committed to developing countries', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_10_1', '17.10.1', 'Worldwide weighted tariff-average', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_11_1', '17.11.1', 'Developing countries’ and least developed countries’ share of global exports', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_12_1', '17.12.1', 'Weighted average tariffs faced by developing countries, least developed countries and small island developing States', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_13_1', '17.13.1', 'Macroeconomic Dashboard', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_14_1', '17.14.1', 'Number of countries with mechanisms in place to enhance policy coherence of sustainable development', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_15_1', '17.15.1', 'Extent of use of country-owned results frameworks and planning tools by providers of development cooperation', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_16_1', '17.16.1', 'Number of countries reporting progress in multi-stakeholder development effectiveness monitoring frameworks that support the achievement of the sustainable development goals', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_17_1', '17.17.1', 'Amount in United States dollars committed to public-private partnerships for infrastructure', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_18_1', '17.18.1', 'Statistical capacity indicators', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_18_2', '17.18.2', 'Number of countries that have national statistical legislation that complies with the Fundamental Principles of Official Statistics', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_18_3', '17.18.3', 'Number of countries with a national statistical plan that is fully funded and under implementation, by source of funding', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_19_1', '17.19.1', 'Dollar value of all resources made available to strengthen statistical capacity in developing countries', 'Active'), ('SDG_INDICATOR_17_19_2', '17.19.2', 'Proportion of countries that (a) have conducted at least one population and housing census in the last 10 years; and (b) have achieved 100 per cent birth registration and 80 per cent death registration', 'Active') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO repo_esd_objectives (esd_objective_id, domain, objective_no, text, status) VALUES ('ESD_SDG01_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner understands the concepts of extreme and relative poverty and is able to critically reflect on their underlying cultural and normative assumptions and practices.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG01_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner knows about the local, national and global distribution of extreme poverty and extreme wealth.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG01_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner knows about causes and impacts of poverty such as unequal distribution of resources and power, colonization, conflicts, disasters caused by natural hazards and other climate change-induced impacts, environmental degradation and technological disasters, and the lack of social protection systems and measures.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG01_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner understands how extremes of poverty and extremes of wealth affect basic human rights and needs.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG01_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner knows about poverty reduction strategies and measures and is able to distinguish between deficit-based and strength-based approaches to addressing poverty.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG01_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to collaborate with others to empower individuals and communities to affect change in the distribution of power and resources in the community and beyond.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG01_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to raise awareness about extremes of poverty and wealth and encourage dialogue about solutions.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG01_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to show sensitivity to the issues of poverty as well as empathy and solidarity with poor people and those in vulnerable situations.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG01_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to identify their personal experiences and biases with respect to poverty.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG01_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to reflect critically on their own role in maintaining global structures of inequality.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG01_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to plan, implement, evaluate and replicate activities that contribute to poverty reduction.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG01_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to publicly demand and support the development and integration of policies that promote social and economic justice, risk reduction strategies and poverty eradication actions.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG01_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to evaluate, participate in and influence decision-making related to management strategies of local, national and international enterprises concerning poverty generation and eradication.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG01_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to include poverty reduction, social justice and anti-corruption considerations in their consumption activities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG01_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to propose solutions to address systemic problems related to poverty.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner knows about hunger and malnutrition and their main physical and psychological effects on human life, and about specific vulnerable groups.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner knows about the amount and distribution of hunger and malnutrition locally, nationally and globally, currently as well as historically.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner knows the main drivers and root causes for hunger at the individual, local, national and global level.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner knows principles of sustainable agriculture and understands the need for legal rights to have land and property as necessary conditions to promote it.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner understands the need for sustainable agriculture to combat hunger and malnutrition worldwide and knows about other strategies to combat hunger, malnutrition and poor diets.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to communicate on the issues and connections between combating hunger and promoting sustainable agriculture and improved nutrition.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to collaborate with others to encourage and to empower them to combat hunger and to promote sustainable agriculture and improved nutrition.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to create a vision for a world without hunger and malnutrition.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to reflect on their own values and deal with diverging values, attitudes and strategies in relation to combating hunger and malnutrition and promoting sustainable agriculture.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to feel empathy, responsibility and solidarity for and with people suffering from hunger and malnutrition.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to evaluate and implement actions personally and locally to combat hunger and to promote sustainable agriculture.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to evaluate, participate in and influence decision-making related to public policies concerning the combat against hunger and malnutrition and the promotion of sustainable agriculture.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to evaluate, participate in and influence decision-making related to management strategies of local, national and international enterprises concerning the combat against hunger and malnutrition and the promotion of sustainable agriculture.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to take on critically their role as an active global citizen in the challenge of combating hunger.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG02_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to change their production and consumption practices in order to contribute to the combat against hunger and the promotion of sustainable agriculture.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner knows conceptions of health, hygiene and well-being and can critically reflect on them, including an understanding of the importance of gender in health and well-being.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner knows facts and figures about the most severe communicable and non-communicable diseases, and the most vulnerable groups and regions concerning illness, disease and premature death.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner understands the socio-political-economic dimensions of health and well-being and knows about the effects of advertising and about strategies to promote health and well-being.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner understands the importance of mental health. The learner understands the negative impacts of behaviours like xenophobia, discrimination and bullying on mental health and emotional well-being and how addictions to alcohol, tobacco or other drugs cause harm to health and well-being.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner knows relevant prevention strategies to foster positive physical and mental health and well-being, including sexual and reproductive health and information as well as early warning and risk reduction.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to interact with people suffering from illnesses, and feel empathy for their situation and feelings.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to communicate about issues of health, including sexual and reproductive health, and well-being, especially to argue in favour of prevention strategies to promote health and well-being.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to encourage others to decide and act in favour of promoting health and well-being for all.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to create a holistic understanding of a life of health and well-being, and to clarify related values, beliefs and attitudes.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to develop a personal commitment to promoting health and well-being for themselves, their family and others, including considering volunteer or professional work in health and social care.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to include health promoting behaviours in their daily routines.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to plan, implement, evaluate and replicate strategies that promote health, including sexual and reproductive health, and well-being for themselves, their families and others.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner has the capacity to perceive when others need help and to seek help for themselves and others.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to publicly demand and support the development of policies promoting health and well-being.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG03_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to propose ways to address possible conflicts between the public interest in offering medicine at affordable prices and private interests within the pharmaceutical industry.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner understands the important role of education and lifelong learning opportunities for all (formal, non-formal and informal learning) as main drivers of sustainable development, for improving people’s lives and in achieving the SDGs.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner understands education as a public good, a global common good, a fundamental human right and a basis for guaranteeing the realization of other rights.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner knows about inequality in access to and attainment of education, particularly between girls and boys and in rural areas, and about reasons for a lack of equitable access to quality education and lifelong learning opportunities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner understands the important role of culture in achieving sustainability.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner understands that education can help create a more sustainable, equitable and peaceful world.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to raise awareness of the importance of quality education for all, a humanistic and holistic approach to education, ESD and related approaches.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able through participatory methods to motivate and empower others to demand and use educational opportunities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to recognize the intrinsic value of education and to analyse and identify their own learning needs in their personal development.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to recognize the importance of their own skills for improving their life, in particular for employment and entrepreneurship.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to engage personally with ESD.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to contribute to facilitating and implementing quality education for all, ESD and related approaches at different levels.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to promote gender equality in education.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to publicly demand and support the development of policies promoting free, equitable and quality education for all, ESD and related approaches as well as aiming at safe, accessible and inclusive educational facilities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to promote the empowerment of young people.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG04_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to use all opportunities for their own education throughout their life, and to apply the acquired knowledge in everyday situations to promote sustainable development.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner understands the concept of gender, gender equality and gender discrimination and knows about all forms of gender discrimination, violence and inequality (e.g. harmful practices such as female genital mutilation, honour killings and child marriage, unequal employment opportunities and pay, language construction, traditional gender roles, gendered impact of natural hazards) and understands the current and historical causes of gender inequality.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner understands the basic rights of women and girls, including their right to freedom from exploitation and violence and their reproductive rights.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner understands levels of gender equality within their own country and culture in comparison to global norms (while respecting cultural sensitivity), including the intersectionality of gender with other social categories such as ability, religion and race.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner knows the opportunities and benefits provided by full gender equality and participation in legislation and governance, including public budget allocation, the labour market and public and private decision-making.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner understands the role of education, enabling technology and legislation in empowering and ensuring the full participation of all genders.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to recognize and question traditional perception of gender roles in a critical approach, while respecting cultural sensitivity.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to identify and speak up against all forms of gender discrimination and debate the benefits of full empowerment of all genders.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to connect with others who work to end gender discrimination and violence, empower those who may still be disempowered and promote respect and full equality on all levels.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to reflect on their own gender identity and gender roles.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to feel empathy and solidarity with those who differ from personal or community gender expectations and roles.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to take the measure of their surroundings to empower themselves or others who are discriminated against because of their gender.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to evaluate, participate in and influence decision-making about gender equality and participation.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to support others in developing empathy across genders and breaking down gender discrimination and violence.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to observe and identify gender discrimination.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG05_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to plan, implement, support and evaluate strategies for gender equality.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner understands water as a fundamental condition of life itself, the importance of water quality and quantity, and the causes, effects and consequences of water pollution and water scarcity.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner understands that water is part of many different complex global interrelationships and systems.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner knows about the global unequal distribution of access to safe drinking water and sanitation facilities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner understands the concept of “virtual water”.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner understands the concept of Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM) and other strategies for ensuring the availability and sustainable management of water and sanitation, including flood and drought risk management.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to participate in activities of improving water and sanitation management in local communities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to communicate about water pollution, water access and water saving measures and to create visibility about success stories.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to feel responsible for their water use.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to see the value in good sanitation and hygiene standards.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to question socio-economic differences as well as gender disparities in the access to safe drinking water and sanitation facilities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to cooperate with local authorities in the improvement of local capacity for self-sufficiency.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to contribute to water resources management at the local level.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to reduce their individual water footprint and to save water practicing their daily habits.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to plan, implement, evaluate and replicate activities that contribute to increasing water quality and safety.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG06_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to evaluate, participate in and influence decision-making on management strategies of local, national and international enterprises related to water pollution.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner knows about different energy resources – renewable and non-renewable – and their respective advantages and disadvantages including environmental impacts, health issues, usage, safety and energy security, and their share in the energy mix at the local, national and global level.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner knows what energy is primarily used for in different regions of the world.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner understands the concept of energy efficiency and sufficiency and knows socio-technical strategies and policies to achieve efficiency and sufficiency.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner understands how policies can influence the development of energy production, supply, demand and usage.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner knows about harmful impacts of unsustainable energy production, understands how renewable energy technologies can help to drive sustainable development and understands the need for new and innovative technologies and especially technology transfer in collaborations between countries.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to communicate the need for energy efficiency and sufficiency.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to assess and understand the need for affordable, reliable, sustainable and clean energy of other people/other countries or regions.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to cooperate and collaborate with others to transfer and adapt energy technologies to different contexts and to share energy best practices of their communities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to clarify personal norms and values related to energy production and usage as well as to reflect and evaluate their own energy usage in terms of efficiency and sufficiency.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to develop a vision of a reliable, sustainable energy production, supply and usage in their country.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to apply and evaluate measures in order to increase energy efficiency and sufficiency in their personal sphere and to increase the share of renewable energy in their local energy mix.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to apply basic principles to determine the most appropriate renewable energy strategy in a given situation.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to analyse the impact and long-term effects of big energy projects (e.g. constructing an off-shore wind park) and energy related policies on different stakeholder groups (including nature).', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to influence public policies related to energy production, supply and usage.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG07_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to compare and assess different business models and their suitability for different energy solutions and to influence energy suppliers to produce safe, reliable and sustainable energy.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner understands the concepts of sustained, inclusive and sustainable economic growth, full and productive employment, and decent work, including the advancement of gender parity and equality, and knows about alternative economic models and indicators.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner has knowledge about the distribution of formal employment rates per sector, informal employment, and unemployment in different world regions or nations, and which social groups are especially affected by unemployment.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner understands the relation between employment and economic growth, and knows about other moderating factors like a growing labour force or new technologies that substitute jobs.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner understands how low and decreasing wages for the labour force and very high wages and profits of managers and owners or shareholders are leading to inequalities, poverty, civil unrest, etc.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner understands how innovation, entrepreneurship and new job creation can contribute to decent work and a sustainability-driven economy and to the decoupling of economic growth from the impacts of natural hazards and environmental degradation.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to discuss economic models and future visions of economy and society critically and to communicate them in public spheres.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to collaborate with others to demand fair wages, equal pay for equal work and labour rights from politicians and from their employer.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to understand how one’s own consumption affects working conditions of others in the global economy.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to identify their individual rights and clarify their needs and values related to work.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to develop a vision and plans for their own economic life based on an analysis of their competencies and contexts.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to engage with new visions and models of a sustainable, inclusive economy and decent work.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to facilitate improvements related to unfair wages, unequal pay for equal work and bad working conditions.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to develop and evaluate ideas for sustainability-driven innovation and entrepreneurship.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to plan and implement entrepreneurial projects.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG08_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to develop criteria and make responsible consumption choices as a means to support fair working conditions and efforts to decouple production from the impact of natural hazards and environmental degradation.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner understands the concepts of sustainable infrastructure and industrialization and society’s needs for a systemic approach to their development.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner understands the local, national and global challenges and conflicts in achieving sustainability in infrastructure and industrialization.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner can define the term resilience in the context of infrastructure and spatial planning, understanding key concepts such as modularity and diversity, and apply it to their local community and nationwide.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner knows the pitfalls of unsustainable industrialization and in contrast knows examples of resilient, inclusive, sustainable industrial development and the need for contingency planning.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner is aware of new opportunities and markets for sustainability innovation, resilient infrastructure and industrial development.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to argue for sustainable, resilient and inclusive infrastructure in their local area.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to encourage their communities to shift their infrastructure and industrial development toward more resilient and sustainable forms.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to find collaborators to develop sustainable and contextual industries that respond to our shifting challenges and also to reach new markets.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to recognize and reflect on their own personal demands on the local infrastructure such as their carbon and water footprints and food miles.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to understand that with changing resource availability (e. g. peak oil, peak everything) and other external shocks and stresses (e. g. natural hazards, conflicts) their own perspective and demands on infrastructure may need to shift radically regarding availability of renewable energy for ICT, transport options, sanitation options, etc.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to identify opportunities in their own culture and nation for greener and more resilient approaches to infrastructure, understanding their overall benefits for societies, especially with regard to disaster risk reduction.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to evaluate various forms of industrialization and compare their resilience.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to innovate and develop sustainable enterprises to respond to their countries’ industrial needs.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to access financial services such as loans or microfinance to support their own enterprises.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG09_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to work with decision-makers to improve the uptake of sustainable infrastructure (including internet access).', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner knows different dimensions of inequality, their interrelations and applicable statistics.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner knows indicators that measure and describe inequalities and understands their relevance for decision-making.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner understands that inequality is a major driver for societal problems and individual dissatisfaction.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner understands local, national and global processes that both promote and hinder equality (fiscal, wage, and social protection policies, corporate activities, etc. ).', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner understands ethical principles concerning equality and is aware of psychological processes that foster discriminative behaviour and decision making.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to raise awareness about inequalities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to feel empathy for and to show solidarity with people who are discriminated against.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to negotiate the rights of different groups based on shared values and ethical principles.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner becomes aware of inequalities in their surroundings as well as in the wider world and is able to recognize the problematic consequences.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to maintain a vision of a just and equal world.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to evaluate inequalities in their local environment in terms of quality (different dimensions, qualitative impact on individuals) and quantity (indicators, quantitative impact on individuals).', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to identify or develop an objective indicator to compare different groups, nations, etc. with respect to inequalities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to identify and analyse different types of causes and reasons for inequalities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to plan, implement and evaluate strategies to reduce inequalities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG10_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to engage in the development of public policies and corporate activities that reduce inequalities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner understands basic physical, social and psychological human needs and is able to identify how these needs are currently addressed in their own physical urban, peri-urban and rural settlements.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner is able to evaluate and compare the sustainability of their and other settlements’ systems in meeting their needs particularly in the areas of food, energy, transport, water, safety, waste treatment, inclusion and accessibility, education, integration of green spaces and disaster risk reduction.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner understands the historical reasons for settlement patterns and while respecting cultural heritage, understands the need to find compromises to develop improved sustainable systems.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner knows the basic principles of sustainable planning and building, and can identify opportunities for making their own area more sustainable and inclusive.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner understands the role of local decision-makers and participatory governance and the importance of representing a sustainable voice in planning and policy for their area.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to use their voice, to identify and use entry points for the public in the local planning systems, to call for the investment in sustainable infrastructure, buildings and parks in their area and to debate the merits of long-term planning.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to connect with and help community groups locally and online in developing a sustainable future vision of their community.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to reflect on their region in the development of their own identity, understanding the roles that the natural, social and technical environments have had in building their identity and culture.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to contextualize their needs within the needs of the greater surrounding ecosystems, both locally and globally, for more sustainable human settlements.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to feel responsible for the environmental and social impacts of their own individual lifestyle.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to plan, implement and evaluate community-based sustainability projects.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to participate in and influence decision processes about their community.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to speak against/for and to organize their voice against/for decisions made for their community.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to co-create an inclusive, safe, resilient and sustainable community.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG11_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to promote low carbon approaches at the local level.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner understands how individual lifestyle choices influence social, economic and environmental development.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner understands production and consumption patterns and value chains and the interrelatedness of production and consumption (supply and demand, toxics, CO2 emissions, waste generation, health, working conditions, poverty, etc. ).', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner knows roles, rights and duties of different actors in production and consumption (media and advertising, enterprises, municipalities, legislation, consumers, etc. ).', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner knows about strategies and practices of sustainable production and consumption.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner understands dilemmas/trade-offs related to and system changes necessary for achieving sustainable consumption and production.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to communicate the need for sustainable practices in production and consumption.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to encourage others to engage in sustainable practices in consumption and production.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to differentiate between needs and wants and to reflect on their own individual consumer behaviour in light of the needs of the natural world, other people, cultures and countries, and future generations.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to envision sustainable lifestyles.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to feel responsible for the environmental and social impacts of their own individual behaviour as a producer or consumer.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to plan, implement and evaluate consumption-related activities using existing sustainability criteria.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to evaluate, participate in and influence decision-making processes about acquisitions in the public sector.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to promote sustainable production patterns.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able take on critically on their role as an active stakeholder in the market.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG12_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to challenge cultural and societal orientations in consumption and production.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner understands the greenhouse effect as a natural phenomenon caused by an insulating layer of greenhouse gases.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner understands the current climate change as an anthropogenic phenomenon resulting from increased greenhouse gas emissions.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner knows which human activities – on a global, national, local and individual level – contribute most to climate change.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner knows about the main ecological, social, cultural and economic consequences of climate change locally, nationally and globally and understands how these can themselves become catalysing, reinforcing factors for climate change.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner knows about prevention, mitigation and adaptation strategies at different levels (global to individual) and for different contexts and their connections with disaster response and disaster risk reduction.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to explain ecosystem dynamics and the environmental, social, economic and ethical impact of climate change.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to encourage others to protect the climate.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to collaborate with others and to develop commonly agreed-upon strategies to deal with climate change.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to understand their personal impact on the world’s climate, from a local to a global perspective.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to recognize that the protection of the global climate is an essential task for everyone and that we need to completely re-evaluate our worldview and everyday behaviours in light of this.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to evaluate whether their private and job activities are climate friendly and – where not – to revise them.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to act in favour of people threatened by climate change.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to anticipate, estimate and assess the impact of personal, local and national decisions or activities on other people and world regions.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to promote climate-protecting public policies.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG13_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to support climate-friendly economic activities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner understands basic marine ecology, ecosystems, predator-prey relationships, etc.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner understands the connection of many people to the sea and the life it holds, including the sea’s role as a provider of food, jobs and exciting opportunities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner knows the basic premise of climate change and the role of the oceans in moderating our climate.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner understands threats to ocean systems such as pollution and overfishing and recognizes and can explain the relative fragility of many ocean ecosystems including coral reefs and hypoxic dead zones.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner knows about opportunities for the sustainable use of living marine resources.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to argue for sustainable fishing practices.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to show people the impact humanity is having on the oceans (biomass loss, acidification, pollution, etc.) and the value of clean healthy oceans.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to influence groups that engage in unsustainable production and consumption of ocean products.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to reflect on their own dietary needs and question whether their dietary habits make sustainable use of limited resources of seafood.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to empathize with people whose livelihoods are affected by changing fishing practices.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to research their country’s dependence on the sea.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to debate sustainable methods such as strict fishing quotas and moratoriums on species in danger of extinction.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to identify, access and buy sustainably harvested marine life, e.g. ecolabel certified products.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to contact their representatives to discuss overfishing as a threat to local livelihoods.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG14_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to campaign for expanding no-fish zones and marine reserves and for their protection on a scientific basis.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner understands basic ecology with reference to local and global ecosystems, identifying local species and understanding the measure of biodiversity.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner understands the manifold threats posed to biodiversity, including habitat loss, deforestation, fragmentation, overexploitation and invasive species, and can relate these threats to their local biodiversity.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner is able to classify the ecosystem services of the local ecosystems including supporting, provisioning, regulating and cultural services and ecosystems services for disaster risk reduction.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner understands the slow regeneration of soil and the multiple threats that are destroying and removing it much faster than it can replenish itself, such as poor farming or forestry practice.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner understands that realistic conservation strategies work outside pure nature reserves to also improve legislation, restore degraded habitats and soils, connect wildlife corridors, sustainable agriculture and forestry, and redress humanity’s relationship to wildlife.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to argue against destructive environmental practices that cause biodiversity loss.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to argue for the conservation of biodiversity on multiple grounds including ecosystems services and intrinsic value.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to connect with their local natural areas and feel empathy with non-human life on Earth.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to question the dualism of human/nature and realizes that we are a part of nature and not apart from nature.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to create a vision of a life in harmony with nature.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to connect with local groups working toward biodiversity conservation in their area.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to effectively use their voice effectively in decision-making processes to help urban and rural areas become more permeable to wildlife through the establishment of wildlife corridors, agro-environmental schemes, restoration ecology and more.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to work with policy-makers to improve legislation for biodiversity and nature conservation, and its implementation.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to highlight the importance of soil as our growing material for all food and the importance of remediating or stopping the erosion of our soils.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG15_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to campaign for international awareness of species exploitation and work for the implementation and development of CITES (Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora) regulations.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner understands concepts of justice, inclusion and peace and their relationship to law.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner understands their local and national legislative and governance systems, how they represent them and that they can be abused through corruption.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner is able to compare their system of justice with those of other countries.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner understands the importance of individuals and groups in upholding justice, inclusion and peace and supporting strong institutions in their country and globally.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner understands the importance of the international human rights framework.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to connect with others who can help them in facilitating peace, justice, inclusion and strong institutions in their country.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to debate local and global issues of peace, justice, inclusion and strong institutions.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to show empathy with and solidarity for those suffering from injustice in their own country as well as in other countries.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to reflect on their role in issues of peace, justice, inclusion and strong institutions.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to reflect on their own personal belonging to diverse groups (gender, social, economic, political, ethnical, national, ability, sexual orientation etc.) their access to justice and their shared sense of humanity.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to critically assess issues of peace, justice, inclusion and strong institutions in their region, nationally and globally.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to publicly demand and support the development of policies promoting peace, justice, inclusion and strong institutions.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to collaborate with groups that are currently experiencing injustice and/or conflicts.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to become an agent of change in local decision-making, speaking up against injustice.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG16_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to contribute to conflict resolution at the local and national level.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_COG_01', 'Cognitive', '1', 'The learner understands global issues, including issues of financing for development, taxation, debt and trade policies, and the interconnectedness and interdependency of different countries and populations.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_COG_02', 'Cognitive', '2', 'The learner understands the importance of global multi-stakeholder partnerships and the shared accountability for sustainable development and knows examples of networks, institutions, campaigns of global partnerships.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_COG_03', 'Cognitive', '3', 'The learner knows the concepts of global governance and global citizenship.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_COG_04', 'Cognitive', '4', 'The learner recognizes the importance of cooperation on and access to science, technology and innovation, and knowledge sharing.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_COG_05', 'Cognitive', '5', 'The learner knows concepts for measuring progress on sustainable development.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_SOC_01', 'Socio-emotional', '1', 'The learner is able to raise awareness about the importance of global partnerships for sustainable development.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_SOC_02', 'Socio-emotional', '2', 'The learner is able to work with others to promote global partnerships for sustainable development and demand governments’ accountability for the SDGs.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_SOC_03', 'Socio-emotional', '3', 'The learner is able to take ownership of the SDGs.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_SOC_04', 'Socio-emotional', '4', 'The learner is able to create a vision for a sustainable global society.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_SOC_05', 'Socio-emotional', '5', 'The learner is able to experience a sense of belonging to a common humanity, sharing values and responsibilities, based on human rights.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_BEH_01', 'Behavioural', '1', 'The learner is able to become a change agent to realize the SDGs and to take on their role as an active, critical and global and sustainability citizen.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_BEH_02', 'Behavioural', '2', 'The learner is able to contribute to facilitating and implementing local, national and global partnerships for sustainable development.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_BEH_03', 'Behavioural', '3', 'The learner is able to publicly demand and support the development of policies promoting global partnerships for sustainable development.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_BEH_04', 'Behavioural', '4', 'The learner is able to support development cooperation activities.', 'Active'), ('ESD_SDG17_BEH_05', 'Behavioural', '5', 'The learner is able to influence companies to become part of global partnerships for sustainable development.', 'Active') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO repo_esd_competencies (esd_competency_id, name, definition, scope, status) VALUES ('ESD_COMP_SYSTEMS_THINKING', 'Systems thinking competency', 'the abilities to recognize and understand relationships; to analyse complex systems; to think of how systems are embedded within different domains and different scales; and to deal with uncertainty.', 'Cross-cutting; relevant to all SDGs', 'Active'), ('ESD_COMP_ANTICIPATORY', 'Anticipatory competency', 'the abilities to understand and evaluate multiple futures – possible, probable and desirable; to create one’s own visions for the future; to apply the precautionary principle; to assess the consequences of actions; and to deal with risks and changes.', 'Cross-cutting; relevant to all SDGs', 'Active'), ('ESD_COMP_NORMATIVE', 'Normative competency', 'the abilities to understand and reflect on the norms and values that underlie one’s actions; and to negotiate sustainability values, principles, goals, and targets, in a context of conflicts of interests and trade-offs, uncertain knowledge and contradictions.', 'Cross-cutting; relevant to all SDGs', 'Active'), ('ESD_COMP_STRATEGIC', 'Strategic competency', 'the abilities to collectively develop and implement innovative actions that further sustainability at the local level and further afield.', 'Cross-cutting; relevant to all SDGs', 'Active'), ('ESD_COMP_COLLABORATION', 'Collaboration competency', 'the abilities to learn from others; to understand and respect the needs, perspectives and actions of others (empathy); to understand, relate to and be sensitive to others (empathic leadership); to deal with conflicts in a group; and to facilitate collaborative and participatory problem solving.', 'Cross-cutting; relevant to all SDGs', 'Active'), ('ESD_COMP_CRITICAL_THINKING', 'Critical thinking competency', 'the ability to question norms, practices and opinions; to reflect on own one’s values, perceptions and actions; and to take a position in the sustainability discourse.', 'Cross-cutting; relevant to all SDGs', 'Active'), ('ESD_COMP_SELF_AWARENESS', 'Self-awareness competency', 'the ability to reflect on one’s own role in the local community and (global) society; to continually evaluate and further motivate one’s actions; and to deal with one’s feelings and desires.', 'Cross-cutting; relevant to all SDGs', 'Active'), ('ESD_COMP_INTEGRATED_PROBLEM_SOLVING', 'Integrated problem-solving competency', 'the overarching ability to apply different problem-solving frameworks to complex sustainability problems and develop viable, inclusive and equitable solution options that promote sustainable development, integrating the above-mentioned competences.', 'Cross-cutting; relevant to all SDGs', 'Active') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO repo_cf_knowledge (cf_knowledge_id, education_level, sub_heading, text, status) VALUES ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_001', 'Secondary education', 'Understanding poverty', 'Poverty as a multidimensional issue, incorporating economic, social and political dimensions.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_002', 'Secondary education', 'Understanding poverty', 'Distinctions between: – absolute (extreme) poverty – for example, living on less than US$2.15/day. – relative poverty – disparities within and between societies. – monetary and multidimensional poverty, considering access to basic needs.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_003', 'Secondary education', 'Understanding poverty', 'Global poverty trends illustrated by comparative statistics and case studies.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_004', 'Secondary education', 'Understanding poverty', 'The relationship between scarcity of resources, economic development, inequality and livelihoods.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_005', 'Secondary education', 'Understanding poverty', 'Household poverty dynamics and the influence of national economic policies on family income and wellbeing.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_006', 'Secondary education', 'Causes and effects', 'Systemic causes of poverty, including: – lack of quality education and decent employment opportunities. – political instability and weak governance. – environmental degradation and climate change. – social exclusion and discrimination.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_007', 'Secondary education', 'Causes and effects', 'Effects of poverty, including:', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_008', 'Secondary education', 'Causes and effects', 'limited access to nutrition, clean water, healthcare, education and safe housing.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_009', 'Secondary education', 'Causes and effects', 'child labour, exploitation and reliance on sweatshops.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_010', 'Secondary education', 'Causes and effects', 'intergenerational poverty and restricted upward mobility.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_011', 'Secondary education', 'Inequality and global context', 'The relationship between poverty, gender and resource distribution, including barriers to education and employment for women and girls, unequal wages, unpaid labour and limited access to finance.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_012', 'Secondary education', 'Inequality and global context', 'The role of inequality in perpetuating poverty, locally and globally.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_013', 'Secondary education', 'Inequality and global context', 'The influence of economic systems and global markets on poverty levels.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_014', 'Secondary education', 'Inequality and global context', 'The contribution of business practices, financial systems and consumer behaviour to poverty cycles and ethical dilemmas.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_015', 'Secondary education', 'Poverty reduction and solutions', 'Roles of governments, global organisations (such as the UN and World Bank) and non-governmental organisations (NGOs) in addressing poverty.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_016', 'Secondary education', 'Poverty reduction and solutions', 'Policy measures for poverty reduction, including social protection, taxation and provision of public services.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_017', 'Secondary education', 'Poverty reduction and solutions', 'Financial planning, inclusive economic models and fair trade as strategies for reducing poverty.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_SEC_018', 'Secondary education', 'Poverty reduction and solutions', 'Entrepreneurship, including youth-and women-led initiatives, and income-generating models such as co-operatives and social enterprises.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_001', 'TVET', 'Poverty', 'Poverty as a multidimensional challenge requiring economic, social, environmental and policy responses.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_002', 'TVET', 'Poverty', 'Absolute and relative poverty in relation to labour markets and livelihoods.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_003', 'TVET', 'Poverty', 'Links between poverty, employment, education and social services.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_004', 'TVET', 'Poverty', 'Effects of poverty on diverse groups (for example, youth, women, informal workers, and persons with disabilities) and its impact on access to decent work and fair wages.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_005', 'TVET', 'Poverty', 'Intersections between poverty, skills gaps, inequality and lack of opportunities in rural and urban economies.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_006', 'TVET', 'Causes and effects', 'Structural causes of poverty in vocational contexts, including: – unemployment, underemployment and low wages. – reliance on informal labour with limited rights and protections. – restricted access to training, finance, markets and infrastructure. – gender-based discrimination and inadequate childcare or support systems.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_007', 'TVET', 'Causes and effects', 'Consequences of poverty, including: – low productivity, poor health outcomes and reduced resilience. – intergenerational poverty driven by lack of skills and limited education.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_008', 'TVET', 'Causes and effects', 'Economic shocks, environmental changes and social exclusion as disruptions to vocational pathways and livelihoods.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_009', 'TVET', 'Inequality and global context', 'Inequality as a barrier to vocational training, job opportunities, technology and capital.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_010', 'TVET', 'Inequality and global context', 'Globalisation, technological change and urbanisation as drivers of income disparities.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_011', 'TVET', 'Inequality and global context', 'Employment trends and poverty levels across sectors, including formal, informal and gig economies.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_012', 'TVET', 'Inequality and global context', 'The role of gender, geography and migration in shaping poverty and livelihoods.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_013', 'TVET', 'Inequality and global context', 'Inclusive economic models, including fair trade, co-operatives, social enterprises, green industries and circular economies.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_014', 'TVET', 'Inequality and global context', 'Labour market needs and vocational pathways linked to entrepreneurship and self-employment.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_015', 'TVET', 'Poverty reduction and solutions', 'The role of TVET in poverty reduction through skills development, employability, entrepreneurship and self-employment.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_016', 'TVET', 'Poverty reduction and solutions', 'Support systems for youth, women and vulnerable groups in achieving decent work.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_017', 'TVET', 'Poverty reduction and solutions', 'Economically and environmentally sustainable enterprises within local and global markets.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_018', 'TVET', 'Poverty reduction and solutions', 'Policy, institutional frameworks and partnerships as enablers of decent work, fair wages and inclusive labour markets.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TVET_019', 'TVET', 'Poverty reduction and solutions', 'TVET as a contributor to resilience in the context of technological change, climate impacts and global economic shifts.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_001', 'Tertiary education', 'Understanding poverty', 'Poverty as a complex, multidimensional phenomenon shaped by economics, power, conflict, inequality, and environmental, social and political systems.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_002', 'Tertiary education', 'Understanding poverty', 'Distinctions between absolute and relative poverty, and between monetary and multidimensional deprivation, with reference to indicators such as the MPI and SDG metrics.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_003', 'Tertiary education', 'Understanding poverty', 'Poverty dynamics among diverse groups, including women, migrants, indigenous peoples, youth and persons with disabilities.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_004', 'Tertiary education', 'Understanding poverty', 'Links between poverty, climate change, environmental degradation and disasters, and their role in vulnerability and exclusion.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_005', 'Tertiary education', 'Causes and effects', 'Structural drivers such as colonial legacies, unequal trade, environmental stressors and labour market exclusion.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_006', 'Tertiary education', 'Causes and effects', 'Contributing factors including unemployment, lack of education and healthcare, displacement and conflict.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_007', 'Tertiary education', 'Causes and effects', 'Impacts on health, education, nutrition, housing, water, sanitation and human security.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_008', 'Tertiary education', 'Causes and effects', 'Economic shocks—pandemics, crises and technological disruptions—as drivers of poverty and inequality.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_009', 'Tertiary education', 'Causes and effects', 'The cyclical relationship between poverty and vulnerability, limiting resilience to crises and climate impacts.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_010', 'Tertiary education', 'Inequality and global context', 'National and global inequality as a factor perpetuating poverty, especially for marginalised groups.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_011', 'Tertiary education', 'Inequality and global context', 'Comparative poverty trends and inequality gaps across countries and regions, using global datasets and case studies.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_012', 'Tertiary education', 'Inequality and global context', 'Intersectionality of gender, race, disability and geography in shaping experiences of poverty and exclusion.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_013', 'Tertiary education', 'Inequality and global context', 'Wealth concentration and tax systems as determinants of mobility and public investment.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_014', 'Tertiary education', 'Inequality and global context', 'The influence of technological change, labour markets and industry trends on livelihoods, digital divides and inequality.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_TER_015', 'Tertiary education', 'Inequality and global context', 'Development cooperation, aid frameworks and pro-poor economic policies (e.g., SDG1, Paris Agreement, Addis Ababa Action Agenda).', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_ADULT_001', 'Adult education', 'Understanding poverty', 'Poverty as a multidimensional issue affecting access to food, water, health services, decent shelter, education, and safe work.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_ADULT_002', 'Adult education', 'Understanding poverty', 'The ways social inequality, gender roles, and financial exclusion deepen poverty.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_ADULT_003', 'Adult education', 'Understanding poverty', 'The impact of conflict, natural disasters, and economic shocks on families and community income.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_ADULT_004', 'Adult education', 'Causes and effects', 'Structural causes of poverty, including unemployment, low wages, limited resources, and systemic discrimination.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_ADULT_005', 'Adult education', 'Causes and effects', 'Interconnections between poverty and poor health, malnutrition, illiteracy, and social exclusion.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_ADULT_006', 'Adult education', 'Causes and effects', 'Long-term effects of poverty on children, families, and societies.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_ADULT_007', 'Adult education', 'Inequality and global context', 'Poverty challenges in local communities compared with those in other regions or countries.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_ADULT_008', 'Adult education', 'Inequality and global context', 'The influence of climate change, gender inequality, and global economic systems on poverty levels.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_ADULT_009', 'Adult education', 'Inequality and global context', 'Variations in access to resources such as land, markets, and finance, and how these shape inequality.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_ADULT_010', 'Adult education', 'Inequality and global context', 'The role of community development agencies, NGOs, and government programmes in addressing poverty.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_ADULT_011', 'Adult education', 'Poverty reduction and sustainable solutions', 'Local and global poverty reduction strategies and their role in supporting household and community development.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_ADULT_012', 'Adult education', 'Poverty reduction and sustainable solutions', 'Local economic systems and the potential role of micro-enterprise in improving livelihoods.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_ADULT_013', 'Adult education', 'Poverty reduction and sustainable solutions', 'Sustainable income-generating opportunities, including small businesses, farming, crafts, services, co-operatives, and green jobs.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG01_ADULT_014', 'Adult education', 'Poverty reduction and sustainable solutions', 'Micro-finance and inclusive business models that support families, such as savings groups, small loans, financial co-operatives, and community funds.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_SEC_001', 'Secondary education', 'Food systems and geography', 'Impact of geography on food production, supply and consumption, including variations in climate, soil, water availability and regional growing seasons.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_SEC_002', 'Secondary education', 'Food systems and geography', 'Influence of geographical and economic factors on local and global food availability and prices.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_SEC_003', 'Secondary education', 'Nutrition and food choices', 'Relationship between food choices and cultural, emotional, environmental, nutritional, religious and social influences.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_SEC_004', 'Secondary education', 'Nutrition and food choices', 'Calculate nutrition requirements based on age, activity level, health status and dietary needs.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_SEC_005', 'Secondary education', 'Nutrition and food choices', 'Long-term health impact of processed foods, dietary trends and fast-food industries.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_SEC_006', 'Secondary education', 'Global hunger and food insecurity', 'Define and measure global hunger using indicators such as undernourishment, stunting and food insecurity.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_SEC_007', 'Secondary education', 'Global hunger and food insecurity', 'Key drivers of hunger, including conflict, poverty, climate change, inequality and market instability.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_SEC_008', 'Secondary education', 'Global hunger and food insecurity', 'International frameworks and strategies aimed at reducing hunger, such as the Right to Food, World Food Programme initiatives and sustainable agriculture.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_SEC_009', 'Secondary education', 'Global hunger and food insecurity', 'Global hunger metrics like the Global Hunger Index (GHI) and Food Insecurity Experience Scale (FIES).', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_SEC_010', 'Secondary education', 'Sustainability and indigenous knowledge', 'The role of indigenous food systems and traditional agricultural practices in promoting sustainability and resilience.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_SEC_011', 'Secondary education', 'Sustainability and indigenous knowledge', 'Economic and environmental factors contributing to food waste and food loss.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_SEC_012', 'Secondary education', 'Sustainability and indigenous knowledge', 'Waste reduction to support broader goals of food security and environmental sustainability.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TVET_001', 'TVET', 'Sustainable food systems', 'Fundamentals of sustainable food systems, encompassing environmental, social and economic dimensions of food production, processing, distribution, preparation and consumption.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TVET_002', 'TVET', 'Sustainable food systems', 'Roles of infrastructure, institutions, people and natural inputs in supporting resilient and efficient food systems.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TVET_003', 'TVET', 'Food safety and nutrition', 'Principles of food safety across the supply chain, including hygiene standards, safe storage, transportation and handling procedures.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TVET_004', 'TVET', 'Food safety and nutrition', 'Basics of nutrition, workforce dietary needs and strategies to ensure food access and wellbeing at workplaces through initiatives like canteens and meal subsidies.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TVET_005', 'TVET', 'Agriculture and rural economies', 'Crop diversification, farm forestry, non-wood forest products and artisanal food production as vital elements of sustainable livelihoods.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TVET_006', 'TVET', 'Agriculture and rural economies', 'Cost structures and management considerations in animal husbandry, including feed alternatives and welfare practices.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TVET_007', 'TVET', 'Food business and market dynamics', 'Economic potential of value-added food products, food tourism and farm-to-fork models for generating income and supporting rural economies.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TVET_008', 'TVET', 'Food business and market dynamics', 'Food tourism to enhance the visibility of local agricultural businesses and create market opportunities.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TVET_009', 'TVET', 'Food business and market dynamics', 'Explore food system entrepreneurship.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TVET_010', 'TVET', 'Community and climate resilience', 'How small-scale farmers can adapt to climate challenges through diversified, sustainable practices.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TVET_011', 'TVET', 'Community and climate resilience', 'Community food audits to identify hunger risks, food security gaps and local opportunities for improvement.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TER_001', 'Tertiary education', 'Food systems and sustainability', 'Key concepts and complex challenges related to global food systems, including the interactions between environmental, social and economic factors.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TER_002', 'Tertiary education', 'Food systems and sustainability', 'Sustainable food systems and their components: natural inputs, production processes, infrastructure, institutions and socio-economic relationships across the food chain.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TER_003', 'Tertiary education', 'Nutrition, diversification and food safety', 'Role of crop diversification and improved nutrition in farm management and food security strategies.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TER_004', 'Tertiary education', 'Nutrition, diversification and food safety', 'Food safety management systems and regulatory frameworks that govern the safe handling, processing, storage and transport of food along the value chain.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TER_005', 'Tertiary education', 'Agricultural innovation and economic development', 'Farm forestry, non-wood forest products and artisanal food production as contributors to food security, environmental protection and rural development.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TER_006', 'Tertiary education', 'Agricultural innovation and economic development', 'Economic impacts of farm-based enterprises and food tourism, including how value-added products open markets and boost local incomes.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TER_007', 'Tertiary education', 'Livestock and workplace nutrition', 'Cost structures, feed alternatives and ethical animal husbandry practices to promote welfare and sustainability.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TER_008', 'Tertiary education', 'Livestock and workplace nutrition', 'Importance of workplace nutrition, meal subsidies and canteen models in promoting workers’ wellbeing and productivity.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TER_009', 'Tertiary education', 'Climate and food security', 'Climate-resilient agriculture techniques, such as agroforestry and conservation tillage, to improve adaptive capacity and sustainability.', 'Active'), ('CFK_SDG02_TER_010', 'Tertiary education', 'Climate and food security', 'Interconnections between climate change, energy systems and food security, including their effects on food availability, access and 